      "sourceStartLine": 1326,
      "content": "\\n\\n     It is also said in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (4.9.17):\\n\\n\\nsaty��i�o hi bhagava�s tava p�da-padmam\\n     �sis tath�nubhajata� puru��rtha-m�rte�\\napy evam arya bhagav�n parip�ti d�n�n\\n     va�reva vatsakam anugraha-k�taro 'sm�n\\n\\n\\n     \"My Lord, O Supreme Lord, You are the supreme personified form of all\\nbenediction. Therefore, for one who abides in Your devotional service with\\nno other desire, worshiping Your lotus feet is better than becoming king\\nand lording it over a kingdom. That is the benediction of worshiping Your\\nlotus feet. To ignorant devotees like me, You are the causelessly merciful\\nmaintainer, just like a cow, who takes care of the newly born calf by\\nsupplying milk and giving it protection from attack.\"*\\n\\n     �r�la �r�dhara Sv�m� comments:\\n\\n     \"This verse means: `O Supreme Personality of Godhead (bhagavan), Your\\nform (murte�) is the supreme bliss that is the highest goal of life\\n(puru��rtha). Your lotus feet (pada-padmam) are the true benediction (satya\\nasih), a benediction far greater that other benedictions (��i�a�),\\nbenedictions such as ruling over a kingdom. That is the right conclusion\\n(hi). Why is that the right conclusion? It is like this (tath�): For the\\ndevotees who worship You (anubhajata�) without any ulterior motive You are\\nthe highest goal of life. O master (�rya),. even though this is so, You\\nstill maintain and protect poor (d�n�n) people like us (asm�n).' \" This\\nverse was spoken by Dhruva to �r� Dhruvapriya (the Supreme Lord's\\nincarnation who was dear to Dhruva).\\n\\n"
