      "content": "\\n\\n     When one directly see the Supreme Personality of Godhead, seeing Him\\noutside the heart is better than seeing Him within the heart. In �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (12.9.5) it is said:\\n\\n\\ng�h�tv�j�dayo yasya\\n     �r�mat-p�d�bja-dar�anam\\nmanas� yoga-pakvena\\n     sa bhav�n me 'k�i-gocara�\\n\\n\\n     \"O Lord whom Brahm� and the demigods saw in their hearts advanced in\\nyoga, You have now come before my eyes.\"\\n\\n     �r�la �r�dhara Sv�m� comments:\\n\\n     \"This verse means: `O Lord whom Brahm� and the demigods saw in their\\nhearts advanced in yoga, You have now come before my eyes. What boon is\\ngreater than this?\"\\n\\n     In �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.12.12) it is also said:\\n\\n\\nyat-p�da-pa��ur bahu-janma-k�cchrata�. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"Who can estimate the transcendental fortune of the residents of\\nV�nd�vana? They were personally visualizing the Supreme Personality of\\nGodhead face to face, He whom many yog�s cannot find even after undergoing\\nsevere austerities, although He is sitting within the heart.\"*\\n\\n     In �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (1.6.33) �r�la N�rada Muni says:\\n\\n\\nprag�yata� sva-v�ry��i\\n     t�rtha-p�da� priya-�rav��\\nah�ta iva me ��ghram\\n     dar�ana� y�ti cetasi\\n\\n\\n     \"The Supreme Lord �r� K���a, whose glories and activities are pleasing\\nto hear, at once appears on the seat of my heart, as if called for, as soon\\nas I begin to chant His holy activities.\"*\\n\\n     Evenb though can always see the Lord within his heart, �r�la N�rada\\nMuni preferred to see Him outside the heart. This In described in these\\nwords of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (11.2.1):\\n\\n\\ngovinda-bhuja-gupt�y��\\n     dv�ravaty�� kur�dvaha\\nav�ts�n n�rado 'bh�k��a�\\n     k���op�sana-l�lasa�\\n\\n\\n     \"Eager to worship Lord K���a, N�rada stayed, O best of the Kurus, at\\nDv�rak�, which is always protected by Lord K���a's arms.\"\\n\\n     This verse was spoken by M�rka��eya Muni to �r� N�r�ya�a ��i.\\n\\n"
