      "headingType": "anuccheda",
      "sourceStartLine": 2578,
      "content": "\\n\\n     Liberation is also described in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(1.6.28):\\n\\n\\nprayujyam�ne mayi t��\\n     �uddh�� bh�gavat�� tanum\\n�rabdha-karma-nirv��o\\n     nyapatat pa�ca-bhautika�\\n\\n\\n     \"Having been awarded a transcendental body befitting an associate of\\nthe Personality of Godhead, I quit the body made of five material elements,\\nand thus all acquired fruitive results of work (karma) stopped.\"*\\n\\n     It is again described in these words of the Supreme Personality of\\nGodhead Himself (�r�mad-Bh�gavatam 1.6.23):\\n\\n\\nhitv�vadyam ima� loka�\\n     gant� maj-janat�m asi\\n\\n\\n     \"By service of the Absolute Truth, even for a few days, a devotee\\nattains firm and fixed intelligence in Me. Consequently he goes to become\\nMy associate in the transcendental world after giving up the present\\ndeplorable material worlds.\"*\\n\\n     In �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 1.6.28 the Supreme Personality of Godhead\\npromises to give the devotee a spiritual form like His own. Here \"t��\\nbh�gavat�m\" means \"a form that is a fragment of the spiritual effulgence of\\nthe Supreme Lord\", {.sy ??168}�uddh�m\" means \"untouched by matter\", {.sy\\n168}tanum\" means \"a form given by the Supreme Personality of Godhead\", and\\n\"mayi prayujyam�ne\" means {.sy 168}attained by me when the results of karma\\ncame to an end\". This happened when the material body made of five elements\\nfell away (nyapatat pa�ca-bhautika�). Here it is seen that the subtle\\nmaterial body of mind, intelligence, and false ego is also destroyed.\\nBecause of his faith in the Supreme Personality of Godhead, the devotee's\\npast karma also comes to an end. In his commentary on this verse �r�la\\n�r�dhara Sv�m� explains:\\n\\n     \"The bodies of a personal associates of the Supreme Lord are eternal,\\npure, and free from karma.\" This verse was spoken by �r� N�rada to �r�\\nVy�sa.\\n\\n"
