      "content": "\\n\\n     Liberation is also eclipsed by associating with great devotees of the\\nLord. This is described in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (4.24.57):\\n\\n\\nk�a��rdhen�pi tulaye\\n     na svarga� n�punar-bhavam\\nbhagavat-sa�gi-sa�gasya\\n     marty�n�� kim ut��i�a�\\n\\n\\n     \"If one by chance associates with a devotee, even for a fraction of a\\nmoment, he no longer is subject to attraction by the results of karma or\\nj��na. What interest, then, can he have in the benedictions of the\\ndemigods, who are subject to the laws of birth and death?\"*\\n\\n     �r�la �r�dhara Sv�m� comments:\\n\\n     \"A person who has attained the feet of a great devotee becomes free of\\nall fear. What remains to be attained by him? Association with a devotee of\\nthe Lord dances on the heads of all other goals of life.\"\\n\\n     This verse was spoken by Lord �iva to the Pracet�s.\\n\\n"
