      "headingType": "anuccheda",
      "sourceStartLine": 4019,
      "content": "\\n\\n     Similar verses are seen in many different places in the scriptures.\\nThat devotional service is the highest attainment is also confirmed in the\\nfollowing words from the B�hat-tantra, words quoted by �r�la Madhv�c�rya in\\nhis commentary:\\n\\n\\nyath� �r�r nitya-mukt�pi\\n     pr�pta-k�m�pi sarvad�\\nup�ste nitya�o vi��um\\n     evam bhakto bhaved api\\n\\n\\n     \"Even though she is eternally liberated, and even though her every\\ndesire is at once fulfilled, Goddess Lak�m� still worships Lord Vi��u\\neternally. The devotees also act in that way.\"\\n\\n     In the Brahma-vaivarta Pur��a it is said:\\n\\n\\nna hr�so na ca v�ddhir v�\\n     mukt�n�� vidyate kvacit\\nvidvat-pratyak�a-siddhatv�t\\n     k�ra��bh�vato 'num�\\n\\n\\n     \"For the liberated souls there is not improvement and no diminution.\\nBecause their knowledge is perfect, they are free from cause and effect.\\n\\n\\nharer up�san� c�tra\\n     sadaiva sukha-r�pi��\\nna ca s�dhana-bh�t� s�\\n     siddhir ev�tra s� yata�\\n\\n\\n     \"In the spiritual world they have forms of bliss. There they worship\\nLord Hari eternally. They do not make gradual advancement in devotional\\nservice, for their devotion is always perfect.\"\\n\\n     In the Saupar�a-�ruti it is said:\\n\\n\\nsarvadaitam up�s�ta, y�vad vimuktir mukt� hy etam up�sate\\n\\n\\n     \"The liberated souls worship Lord Hari eternally. The goddess of\\nliberation herself worships Lord Hari.\"\\n\\n     In his Bh�rata-t�tparya commentary on Mah�bh�rata, �r�la Madhv�c�rya\\nquotes these words from another place in the �ruti-��stra:\\n\\n\\nmukt�n�m pai bhaktir hi\\n     param�nanda-r�pi��\\n\\n\\n     \"The liberated souls also engage in devotional service. It brings them\\ngreat bliss.\"\\n\\n     This truth is also confirmed by the following words of the Gautam�ya\\nTantra:\\n\\n\\neva� d�k��� cared yas tu\\n     puru�o vita-kalma�a�\\nsa loke vartam�no 'pi\\n     j�van-mukta� pramodate\\n\\n\\n     \"A sinless person initiated by a bona-fide spiritual master becomes\\nliberated. Even as he lives in the material world he is both liberated and\\nhappy.\\n\\n\\nudit�k�tir �nanda�\\n     sarvatra sama-dar�aka�\\np�r��hant�-may� s�k��d\\n     bhakti� sy�t prema-lak�a��\\n\\n\\n     \"He becomes bliss personified. He sees with equal vision. Retaining\\nhis individual identity, he serves the Lord with great love and devotion.\"\\n\\n     The equal vision mentioned here means that the devotees are equal in\\nboth loss and gain. In the Gautam�ya Tantra the sages ask this question:\\n\\n\\nkatha� bhaktir bhavet prem��\\n     j�van-muktasya n�rada\\nj�van-mukta-�ar�r����\\n     cit-satt�-ni�sp�h� yata�\\nvirakte� k�ra�a� bhakti�\\n     s� tu muktes tu s�dhanam\\n\\n\\n     \"Why would a soul liberated in this life serve the Supreme Lord with\\nlove and devotion? The souls already liberated in this life have already\\nattained eternal liberated life. Therefore they have no material desires.\\nDevotional service is only a means to attain an end, to attain\\nrenunciation, or to attain liberation.\"\\n\\n     To this question �r� N�rada gives the following answer:\\n\\n\\nbhadra-mukta� bhavadbhi� ca\\n     muktis tury� par�t par�\\nniraha� yatra cit-satt�\\n     tury� s� muktir ucyate\\n\\n\\n     \"You are all perfectly liberated. Liberation is beyond the material\\nworld. It is higher than the highest. Spiritual existence where individual\\nidently no longer exists is called liberation.\\n\\n\\np�r��hant�-may� bhaktis\\n     tury�t�t� nigadyate\\nk���a-dh�mamaya� brahma\\n     kvacit kutr�pi bh�sate\\n\\n\\n     \"However, individual identity continues to exist in devotional\\nservice, which is said to be above even liberation. The impersonal Brahman\\neffulgence that is the goal of liberation is only the effulgence of Lord\\nK���a's limbs.\\n\\n\\nnirv�jendriya-ga� tat tu\\n     �tma-stha� kevala� sukham\\nk���as tu parip�r��tm�\\n     sarvatra sukha-r�paka�\\nbhakti-v�tti-k�t�bhy�s�t\\n     tat-k�a��d gocar�-k�ta�\\n\\n\\n     \"Spiritual bliss is perceived only by spiritual senses. Lord K���a is\\nthe original form of the Supreme. He is always full of bliss. By regularly\\nserving Him with devotion one can come to see Him directly.\"\\n\\n     Even the impersonalist philosophers accept the supreme position of the\\nLord's personal form. In the N�si�ha-t�pan� Upani�ad (2.4) it is said:\\n\\n\\nya� vai sarve dev� �mananti mumuk�avo brahma-v�dina� ca\\n\\n\\n     \"The demigods, the brahmav�d�s, and the j��n�s who long for liberation\\nall bow down before the Supreme Personality of Godhead.\"\\n\\n     In his commentary on that verse �r� �a�kar�c�rya says:\\n\\n\\nyath� mukt� api l�lay� vigraha� k�tv� bhagavanta� bhajante\\n\\n\\n     \"The liberated souls attain spiritual bodies, worship the Supreme\\nPersonality of Godhead and participate in His pastimes.\"\\n\\n     The word \"brahma-v�dina�\" here means \"liberated souls\". This is\\nsupported by these words of P��ini (A���dhy�y� 7.2.7):\\n\\n\\nvada sthairye\\n\\n\\n     That the impersonalist j��n�s eventually become devotees is also\\nconfiremd by these words (Bhagavad-g�t� 7.17):\\n\\n\\nte��� j��n� nitya-yukta\\n     eka-bhaktir vi�i�yate\\n\\n\\n     \"Of these, the wise one who is in full knowledge in union with Me\\nthrough pure devotional service is the best.\"*\\n\\n     That the mercy of the Supreme Personality of Godhead is the highest\\nattainemnt is confirmed by the following words of the N�rada-pa�car�tra,\\nJit�nta-stotra:\\n\\n\\nmok�a-s�lokya-s�r�py�n\\n     pr�rthaye na dhar�dhara\\nicch�mi hi mah�-bh�ga\\n     k�ru�yam tava suvrata\\n\\n\\n     \"O Lord, O maintainer of the worlds, I do not pray for liberation, or\\nto live on Your planet, or to have a from like Your form. I wish only for\\nYour mercy.\"\\n\\n     That devotional service eclipses all other goals of life is confirmed\\nby these words of �r� Haya��r�a-pa�car�tra, �r� N�r�ya�a-vy�ha-stava:\\n\\n\\nna dharma� k�mam artha� v�\\n     mok�a� v� varade�vara\\npr�rthaye tava p�d�bje\\n     d�syam ev�bhik�maye\\n\\n\\n     \"O Supreme Personality of Godhead, O giver of boons, I do not pray for\\npiety, sense pleasure, or wealth. I wish only service to Your feet.\\n\\n\\npuna� punar var�n ditsur\\n     vi��ur mukti� na y�cita�\\nbhaktir eva v�t� yena\\n     prahl�da� ta� nam�my aham\\n\\n\\n     \"I offer my respectful obeisances to �r� Prahl�da. Even though Lord\\nVi��u again and again offered boons to him, he never asked for liberation.\\nThe boons he chose were only devotional service.\\n\\n\\nyad�cchay� labdham api\\n     vi��or d��arathes tu ya�\\nnaicchan moksa� vin� d�sya�\\n     tasmai hanumate nama�\\n\\n\\n     \"I offer my respectful obeisances to �r� Hanum�n. Even though Lord\\nR�macandra offered him liberation, he would not accept it without\\ndevotional service.\"\\n\\n     In the Jit�nta-stotra it is also said:\\n\\n\\ndharm�rtha-k�ma-mok�e�u\\n     necch� mama kad�cana\\ntvat-p�da-pa�kajasy�dho\\n     j�vita� d�yat�� mama\\n\\n\\n     \"O Lord, never I will wish for material piety, sense pleasure, or\\nmoney. Please give me only a place under Your lotus feet.\"\\n\\n     It is not surprising that love for the Supreme Lord eclipses all other\\ngoals of life. In �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (5.18.12) it is said:\\n\\n\\nyasy�sti bhaktir bhagavaty aki�can�\\n     sarvair gu�ais tatra sam�sate sur��\\n\\n\\n     \"All the demigods and their exalted qualities, such as religion,\\nknowledge, and renunciation, become manifest in the body of one who has\\ndeveloped unalloyed devotion for the Supreme Personality of Godhead,\\nV�sudeva.\"*\\n\\n     Devotional service brings the virtue of compassion. In �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (9.21.12) King Rantideva says:\\n\\n\\nna k�maye 'ha� gatim ��var�t par�m\\n     a��arddhi-yukt�m apunar-bhava� v�\\n�rtim prapadye 'khila-deha-bh�j�m\\n     anta�-sthito yena bhavanty adu�kh��\\n\\n\\n     \"I do not pray to the Supreme Personality of Godhead