      "content": "\\n\\n     Love for the Supreme Personality of Godhead is ultimate result\\nobtained by following the spiritual practices described in the Vedas. It is\\nsaid in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (3.9.41):\\n\\n\\np�rtena tapas� yaj�air\\n     d�nair yoga-sam�dhin�\\nr�ddha� ni��reyas�� pu�s��\\n     mat-pr�tis tattvavin-matam\\n\\n\\n     \"It is the opinion of expert transcendentalists that the ultimate goal\\nof performing all traditional good works, penances, sacrifices, charities,\\nmystic activities, trances, etc. is to invoke My satisfaction.\"*\\n\\n     �r�la �r�dhara Sv�m� comments:\\n\\n     \"In this verse the Supreme Personality of Godhead says: `Nothing is\\nmore important than satisfying Me.' He says: `It is the opinion of expert\\ntranscendentalists (tattvavin-matam) that the ultimate goal (r�ddha�\\nni��reyas�m) of performing all traditional good works (beginning with\\np�rta) is to invoke My satisfaction (mat-pr�ti�)'.\"\\n\\n     The meaning here is that persons who are not great transcendentalists,\\npersons who do not know the real truth, think other results are more\\nimportant than satisfying the Supreme Personality of Godhead. These persons\\nthink devotional service is only a tool that one uses to perform these\\nother activities.\\n\\n"
