      "headingType": "anuccheda",
      "sourceStartLine": 4558,
      "content": "\\n\\n     The devotees are also praised in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(11.14.24):\\n\\n\\nv�g gadagad� dravate yasya citta�\\n     rudaty abh�k��a� hasati kvacic ca\\nvilajja udg�yati n�tyate ca\\n     mad-bhakti-yukto bhuvana� pun�ti\\n\\n\\n     \"A devotee whose voice becomes choked, whose heart melts, who weeps\\nagain and again, who becomes embarrassed, and who sometimes laughs, sings,\\nand dances, purifies the whole world.\"\\n\\n     The meaning of this verse is clear.\\n\\n"
    },
    {
      "number": 38,
      "sub": null,
      "sourceLabel": "Anuccheda 38",
      "headingType": "anuccheda",
      "sourceStartLine": 4578,
      "content": "\\n\\n     The Supreme Lord Himself praises the devotees in these words of �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (11.14.16):\\n\\n\\nnirapek�a� muni� ��nta�\\n     nirvaira� sama-dar�anam\\nanuvraj�my aha� nitya�\\n     p�yeyety a�ghri-re�ubhi�\\n\\n\\n     \"I follow a devotee who is peaceful and desireless, who always thinks\\nof Me, who sees everyone equally. and who thinks of no one as his enemy. I\\nfollow him so I may become purified by the dust of his feet.\"\\n\\n     In this verse the Supreme Lord saus: \"I follow a pure devotee (muni),\\na devotee like �r� N�rada and others, a devotee who is peaceful (��ntam)\\nand desireless (nirapek�am), who does not think some things should be\\naccepted and others should be rejected (sama-dar�anam). and who thinks of\\nno one as his enemy (nirvairam).\"\\n\\n     In this verse the Supreme Lord says: \"I am devoted to the saintly\\npersons who have sincere devotion to Me.\" Why does the Lord follow such\\ndevotees. The Lord says: \"I follow them so I may become absolved (p�yeya)\\nof the debt I owe them for their devotion to Me\". That is the meaning here.\\nthis verse was spoken by the Supreme Personality of Godhead.\\n\\n"
    },
    {
