      "headingType": "anuccheda",
      "sourceStartLine": 5290,
      "content": "\\n\\n     In the account of the Vi��u Pur��a, �r� Prahl�da, although praying to\\nattain love for the Lord, is not averse to residing in the material world.\\nHe says (Vi��u Pur��a 1.20.18, 19, 26, and 27):\\n\\n\\nn�tha yoni-sahasre�u\\n     ye�u ye�u vraj�my aham\\nte�u te�v acyut� bhaktir\\n     acyute 'stu sad� tvayi\\n\\n\\n     \"O Lord, I pray that I will always have unflinching devotion to You,\\neven if I must take take birth in thousands of wombs in this world,\\n\\n\\ny� pr�tir avivek�n��\\n     vi�aye�v anap�yin�\\ntv�m anusmarata� s� me\\n     h�day�n n�pasrpatu\\n\\n\\n     \"Fools fall in love with material sense objects. As they always love\\nsenses obejcts, may I always love You. I always meditate on You. I pray\\nthat You will never leave my heart.\"\\n\\n\\nk�ta-k�tyo 'smi bhagavan\\n     vare��nena yat tvayi\\nbhavitr� tvat-pras�dena\\n     bhaktir avyabhic�ri��\\n\\n\\n     \"O Supreme Personality of Godhead, please give me the boon that by\\nYour mercy I will always have unflinching devotion to You. With this boon\\nmy life will be successful.\\n\\n\\ndharm�rtha-k�mai� ki� tasya\\n     muktis tasya kare sthit�\\nsamasta-jagat�� m�le\\n     yasya bhakti� sthir� tvayi\\n\\n\\n     \"What to speak of piety, econimoc development, sense gratification,\\neven liberation stands in the hand of anyone who has firm devotion to You,\\nthe root from which all the worlds have grown.\"\\n\\n     To these words the Supreme Personality of Godhead gave this reply\\n(Vi��u Pur��a 1.20.28):\\n\\n\\nyath� te ni�cala� ceto\\n     mayi bhakti-samanvitam\\ntath� tvam mat-pras�dena\\n     nirv��a� param �psyasi\\n\\n\\n     \"Because your heart has unflinching devotion to Me, by My mercy you\\nwill attain final liberation.\"\\n\\n     This last verse means: \"to the extent that you have unlfinching\\ndevotion to Me, to that extent You are qualified to serve My feet.\" This\\nsame idea is also seen in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (5.14.44):\\n\\n\\nsev�nurakta-manas�m abhavo 'pi phalgu�\\n\\n\\n     \"Indeed, even liberation is considered insignificant for those whose\\nminds are attracted to the loving service of the Lord.\"*\\n\\n     This same meaning is also hinted in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(11.2.8):\\n\\n\\naha� kila pur�nanta�\\n     praj�rtho bhuvi mukti-dam\\nap�jaya� na mok��ya\\n     mohito deva-m�yay�\\n\\n\\n     \"Wishing a child, I long ago worshiped the limitlsess Supreme Lord,\\nwho can give the gift of liberation. Bewildered by the Lord's illusory\\npotency, I did not worship Him to attain liberation.\"\\n\\n     This verse means: \"Wishing a child, Im my own expanded form, where I\\nbore the name Sutap�, I long ago worshiped (ap�jayam) the limitlsess\\nSupreme Lord, who can give the gift of liberation (muktidam). I did not\\nworship Him to attain liberation. Bewildered (mohita�) by the Lord's (deva)\\nmerciful (m�yay�) glance, I desired to have a son.\" Here the word \"m�y�\"\\nmeans \"mercy\". In the Vi�va-prak��a Dictionary it is said:\\n\\n\\nm�y� dambhe k�p�y�� ca\\n\\n\\n     \"The word `m�y�' may mean `trickery' or `mercy'.\"\\n\\n     In �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 11.2.8 the word \"kila\" (indeed) means \"the\\nSupreme Personality of Godhead's words in the maternity room prove all\\nthis\". It is also said in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (11.2.9):\\n\\n\\nyath� vicitra-vyasan�t. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"O saintly spiritual master, please teach me how I may become free\\nfrom this fearful material world filled with dangers.\"\\n\\n     In this verse the word \"vyasana\" (danger) mans {.sy 168}the dangers\\nthat come from being separated from the Supreme Lord\" and the word \"bhaya\"\\n(fear) means \"the fears that come fromk being separated from the Supreme\\nLord\". It is also said in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (11.2.33):\\n\\n\\nmanye kuta�cit. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"I think devotional service to the lotus feet of the infallible\\nSupreme Personality of Godhead is the only way a person whose heart is\\nalways agitated, a person who thinks his external material body is his true\\nself, can become free from all fear. When devotional service is present\\nfears come to an end.\"\\n\\n     �r� N�rada explains (�r�mad-Bh�gavatam 11.5.45):\\n\\n\\ntvam apy et�n. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"O very fortunate one, by faithfully following the path of devotional\\nservice you have now heard, you will become liberated and will attain the\\nSupreme.\"\\n\\n     Here the word \"vi�va\" shows that by ataining the Supreme Personality\\nof Godhead one becomes free from both fears and dancers that come from His\\nabsence. At the end of this conversation it is said (�r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n11.5.54):\\n\\n\\ntvam apy et�n. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"O fortunate one, by faithfully following this path you have heard\\nfrom me, this path of worshipping the Supreme Personality of Godhead, you\\nwill become liberated and will attain the Supreme.\"\\n\\n     In this verse and the verse following it the way to attain association\\nwith Lord K���a is described. �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 11.2.8, which was quoted in\\nthis anuccheda, was spoken by �r� Vasudeva Mah�r�ja to �r� N�rada.\\n\\n"
