      "content": "\\n\\n     Uddhava thinks: \"For me to aspire to become like the gop�s is like a\\ndwarf yearning to catch the moon. Therefore my only prayer is this: (�r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam 10.47.61):\\n\\n\\n�s�m aho cara�a-re�u-ju��m aha� sy��\\n     v�nd�vane kim api gulma-latau�adh�n�m\\ny� dustyaja� sva-janam �rya-patha� ca hitv�\\n     bhejur mukunda-padav�� �rutibhir vim�gyam\\n\\n\\n     \"The gop�s of V�nd�vana have given up the association of their\\nhusbands, sons, and other family members, who are very difficult to give\\nup, and they have forsaken the path of chastity to take shelter of tyhe\\nlotus feet of Mukunda, K���a, which one should search for by Vedic\\nknowledge. Oh, let me be fortunate enough to be one of the bushes,\\ncreepers, or herbs in V�nd�vana, because the gop�s trample them and bless\\nthem with the dust of their feet.\"*\\n\\n     In this verse Uddhava says: \"It is not possible for me to attain even\\na slight touch of the effulgent glory of the gop�s' great love for Lord\\nK���a. Therefore my desire will be to tak another, a different birth in\\nthis world. If in that birth I still cannot directly attain the touch of\\nthe gop�s' feet, for what shall I pray? I will pray: Let me take birth\\n(sy�m) even among the undesireable speciies of life, among the bushes,\\ncreepers, or herbs (kim api gulma-latau�adh�n�m), for then I will have the4\\ngood fortune of attaining the touch of the dust of the gop�s' feet (�s�m\\ncara�a-re�u).\" Here the word {.sy 168}aho\" (Oh!) shows that Uddhava's heart\\nis agitated with this desire. Here the question may be asked: \"What is the\\nnature of these gop�s?\" The answer is given: \"Impelled by passionate love,\\nthey have forsaken the path of chastity and rejected the moral codes taught\\nby the Vedas and ordinary social custon\" (y� dustyaja� sva-janam �rya-\\npatha� ca hitv�). They follow the blissful path of love for Lord K���a, a\\npath all the �ruti-��stras have concluded is the crest jewel of all goals\\nof life (bhejur mukunda-padav�� �rutibhir vim�gyam).\" The conclusion, then,\\nof this verse is: \"Let us also reject the path of conventional religion\\n(�rya-patham) and follow the footsteps of the gop�s.\"\\n\\n"
