      "content": "\\n\\n     Humbled by seeing the gop�s' glorious status, and feeling himself very\\nunqualified, Uddhava offers respectful obeisances to the dust of the gop�s'\\nfeet. He says in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.47.63):\\n\\n\\nvande nanda-vraja-str����\\n     p�da-re�um abhik�na�a�\\ny�s�� hari-kathodg�ta�\\n     pun�ti bhuvana-trayam\\n\\n\\n     \"I repeatedly offer my respects to the dust from the feet of the women\\nof Nanda Maharaja's cowherd village. When these gop�s loudly chant the\\nglories of �r� K���a, the vibration purifies the three worlds.\"***\\n\\n     In this verse Uddhava says: \"I offer my respectful obeisances (vande)\\nto the dust of the gop�s' feet (p�da-re�um).\" Then in the second part of\\nthe verse he describes the gop�s. Uddhava's meaning here is: \"The good\\nfortune we have attained today is very wonderful.\" Lord K���a Himself\\ndescribes the glories of His devotees in these words of Padma Pur��a,\\nK�rttika-m�h�tmya:\\n\\n\\nete hi y�dav�� sarve\\n     mad-ga�� eva bh�vini\\nsarvad� mat-priy� devi\\n     mat-tulya-gu�a-��lina�\\n\\n\\n     \"O glorious goddess, all the Y�davas are always very dear to Me. They\\nhave virtues like My own.\"\\n\\n     The Y�davas, who are very dear to Lord K���a, the Supreme Personality\\nof Godhead, is confirmed by these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.90.46):\\n\\n\\n�ayy�san��an�l�pa. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"The V���is were so absorbed in K���a consciousness that they forgot\\ntheir own bodies while sleeping, sitting, walking, conversing, playing,\\nbathing, and so on.\"***\\n\\n     Devotees whose relationship is with other forms of the Lord, forms\\nother than the form of Lord K���a, are not as glorious as the Y�davas. That\\namongst the Y�davas and other devotees Uddhava is very glorious is\\nconfirmed by these words spoken by Lord K���a Himself in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(11.16.29):\\n\\n\\ntva� tu bh�gavate�v aham\\n\\n\\n     \"O Uddhava, amongst the devotees you are my representative.\"\\n\\n     Lord K���a also says in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (11.11.49):\\n\\n\\ntva� me bh�tya� suh�t sakh�\\n\\n\\n     \"O Uddhava, you are My friend, servant, and well-wisher.\"\\n\\n     Lord K���a also says in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (3.4.31):\\n\\n\\nnoddhavo 'nv api man-ny�na�\\n\\n\\n     \"Udsdhava is not inferior to Me in any way.\"*\\n\\n     Lord K���a also says in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (11.14.15):\\n\\n\\nna ca sa�kar�a�o na �r�r\\n     naiv�tm� ca yath� bhav�n\\n\\n\\n     \"My dear Uddhava, neither Lord Brahm�, Lord �iva, Lord Sa�kar�a�a, the\\ngoddess of fortune, nor indeed My own self are as dear to Me as you.\"***\\n\\n     In these and many other statements Lord K���a affirms that Uddhava is\\nexalted amongst the devotees. Still, Uddhava is very humble when he speaks\\nabout the gop�s. He is not humble in the same way about the Lord's queens\\nin Dv�rak�. The queens' glory compares to the gop�s' glory in the same way\\nthe eye of a person blind from birth compares to the glory of the full\\nmoon.\\n\\n"
