      "content": "\\n\\n     �r� R�dh�-dev� is described in these words of the Adi Pur��a:\\n\\n\\ntrailokye p�thiv� dhany�\\n     tatra v�nd�vana� puna�\\ntatr�pi gopik�� p�rtha\\n     tatra r�dh�bhidh� mama\\n\\n\\n     \"O P�rtha, the earth planet is the most fortunate place in the three\\nworlds, for V�nd�vana forest, the gop�s, and My beloved who bears the name\\nR�dh� all stay there.\"\\n\\n     �r� R�dh�-dev� is AGAIN described in these words of the Padma Pur��a,\\nK�rttika-m�h�tmya:\\n\\n\\nyath� r�dh� priy� vi��os\\n     tasy�� ku��a� priya� tath�\\nsarva-gop��u saivaik�\\n     vi��or atyanta-vallabh�\\n\\n\\n     \"Just as �r�mat� R�dh�r��� is dear to the Supreme Lord K���a (Vi��u),\\nso Her bathing place (R�dh�-ku��a) is equally dear to K���a. Among all the\\ngop�s, She alone stands supreme as the Lord's most beloved.\"*\\n\\n     �r� R�dh�'s love is the greatest. This is confirmed in the following\\nwords of the Agni Pur��a, V�san�-bh��ya:\\n\\n\\ngopya� papracchur u�asi\\n     k����nucaram uddhavam\\nhari-l�l�-vih�r��� ca\\n     tatraik�� r�dhik�� vin�\\nr�dh� tad-bh�va-saml�n�\\n     v�san�y� vir�mit�\\n\\n\\n     \"At dawn the gop�s asked K���a's servant Uddhava to describe how K���a\\nwas enjoying pastimes without �r� R�dh�. At that moment, overcome with love\\nand yearning to be with K���a, �r� R�dh� fainted.\"\\n\\n     Here the words \"v�san�y� vir�mit�\" indicate that �r� R�dh� was in the\\nninth state of consciousness. In other words, She was completely overcome.\\nShe had no power to continue. That �r� R�dh� is the best of the gop�s is\\nseen in the following words describing the r�sa-dance pastime in �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (10.30.27):\\n\\n\\nkasy�� pad�ni. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"Here we see the footprints of some gop� who must have been walking\\nalong with the son of Nanda Mah�r�ja. He must have put His arm on Her\\nshoulder, just as an elephant rests His trunk on the shoulder of an\\naccompanying she-elephant.\"***\\n\\n     These words describe �r� R�dh�'s supreme good fortune. �r� R�dh�'s\\nname is indirectly uttered in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.30.28):\\n\\n\\nanay�r�dhito n�na�\\n     bhagav�n harir ��vara�\\nyan no vih�ya govinda�\\n     pr�to y�m anayad raha�\\n\\n\\n     \"Certainly this particular gop� has perfectly worshiped (�r�dhita) the\\nall-powerful Personality of Godhead, Govinda, since He was so pleased with\\nHer that He abandoned the rest of us and brought Her to a secluded\\nplace.\"***\\n\\n     Here the words \"anaya bhagavan radhitah\" mean {.sy 168}�r� R�dh�\\nbrought the Supreme Personality of Godhead under Her control\". The word\\n\"n�nam\" here is used in the sense of making a guess. Within the word\\n\"�r�dhita�\" (worshiped) in this verse the name R�dh� is hidden. The result\\nof R�dh�'s worshiping K���a is given in the words beginning with \"yan na\",\\nthe words that say: \"He was so pleased with Her that He abandoned the rest\\nof us and brought Her to a secluded place.\" Here the word \"govinda�\" refers\\nto Lord K���a, the king of Gokula. This verse was spoken by the vraja-\\ngop�s.\\n\\n"
