      "content": "\\n\\n\\n     The devotees dear to the Lord are described in these words of �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (1.18.13):\\n\\n\\ntulay�ma laven�pi. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"The value of a moment's association with the devotee of the Lord\\ncannot be compared to the attainment of heavenly planets or liberation from\\nmatter, and what to speak of worldly benedictions in the form of material\\nprosperity, which are for those who are meant for death.\"*\\n\\n     In this way it is seen that the Supreme Personality of Godhead is the\\nobject of love (vi�aya) and He is also the primary cause (�lambana) that\\nmakes the devotees fall in love with Him. By following the path that begins\\nwith hearing about the Lord, the devotees attain love (pr�ti) for Him. The\\nword \"vi�aya\" may mean either the person who loves or the person who is\\nloved. It is said in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (1.16.5-6):\\n\\n\\ntat kathyat�� mah�-bh�ga\\n     yadi k���a-kath��rayam\\nathav�sya pad�mbhoja-\\n     makaranda-lih�� sat�m\\n\\n\\n     \"Please describe all these incidents if they realte to the topics of\\nLord K���a. The devotees of the Lord are accustomed to licking up the honey\\navailable from the lotus feet of the Lord.\"*\\n\\n     By associating with the Supreme Lord, one falls in love with Him. In\\nthis way the Supreme Personality of Godhead is the primary cause (�lambana)\\nof ecstatic love for Him. The secondary causes (udd�pana) of ecstatic love\\nare different. The Lord's dear devotees, who are of two kinds, namely the\\ndevotees who have the same desire (sav�sana) and the devotees who have\\ndifferent desires (bhinna-v�sana), are also objects (vi�aya) of ecstatic\\nlove. The devotees are also the reservoirs of love (�dh�ra) for the Lord.\\nHowever, one's material friends and kinsmen are not the causes of attaining\\nlove ofr Lord K���a. Indeed, the devotees do not pray to attain love for\\ntheir friends and kinsmen. Rthaer they pray only to love the Supreme Lord.\\nThat they do not pray to attain love for their friends and kinsmen is seen\\nin these words of Queen Kunt� in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (1.8.41):\\n\\n\\natha vi�ve�a vi�v�tman\\n     vi�va-m�rte sva-kesu me\\nsneha-p��am ima� chindhi\\n     d�dha� p��dusu v�s�isu\\n\\n\\n     \"O Lord of the universe, soul of the universe, O personality of the\\nform of the universe, please, therefore, sever my tie of affection for my\\nkinsmen, the Pa��avas and the Vr��is.\"*\\n\\n"
