      "content": "\\n\\n     The love the devotees accept (a�g�k�ra) is described in these words of\\nQueen Kunt� in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (1.8.43):\\n\\n\\n�r�-k�s�a k�s�a-sakha v���y-rsabh�vani-dhrug-\\n     r�janya-va��a-dahan�napavarga-v�rya\\ngovinda go-dvija-sur�rti- har�vat�ra\\n     yoge�var�khila-guro bhagavan namas te\\n\\n\\n     \"O K���a, O friend of Arjuna, O chief amongst the descendants of\\nV���i, You are the destroyer of those political parties which are\\ndisturbing elements on this earth. Your prowess never deteriorates. You are\\nthe proprietor of the transcendental abode, and You descend to relieve the\\ndistresses of the cows, the br�hmanas and the devotees. You possess all\\nmystic powers, and You are the preceptor of the entire universe. You are\\nthe almighty God, and I offer You my respectful obeisances.\"***\\n\\n     Here Kunt� calls out to K���a, addressing Him with names such as \"O\\nfriend of Arjuna (K���a-sakha). In this context Queen Kunt� accepts a\\nloving relationship with Arjuna and others because they are all filled with\\nlove for the Supreme Lord. These verses were spoken by Queen Kunt� to the\\nSupreme Personality of Godhead, Lord K���a.\\n\\n"
