      "headingType": "anuccheda",
      "sourceStartLine": 8145,
      "content": "\\n\\n     Now we may consider these words spoken by Uddhava in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(11.29.39-40):\\n\\n\\nv�k�a� ca me su-d��ha� sneha-p��o\\n     d���rha-v���y-andhaka-s�tvate�u\\npras�rita� s���i-viv�ddhaye tvay�\\n     sva-m�yay� hy �tma-subodha-hetin�\\n\\n\\n     \"The firmly bindfing rope of my affection for the families of the\\nDa��rhas, V���is, Andhakas, and S�tvatas-a rope You originally cast over me\\nby Your illusory energy for the purpose of developing Your creation-is now\\ncut off by the weapon of transcendental knowledge of the self.***\\n\\n\\nnamo 'stu te mah�-yogin\\n     prapannam anu��dhi m�m\\nyath� tvac-cara��mbhoje\\n     rati� sy�d anap�yin�\\n\\n\\n     \"Obeisances unto You, O greatest of yog�s. Please instruct me, who am\\nsurrendered unto You, how I may have undeviating attachment to Your lotus\\nfeet.\"***\\n\\n     Here Uddhava says: \"The rope of my affection for others in a bodily\\nrelationshoip with me, a rope You originally cast over me by Your illusory\\nenergy for the purpose of developing Your creation-is now cut off.\" How was\\nthat rope cut off? The answer is given in the words: \"by the weapon of\\ntranscendental knowledge of the self.\" This means \"by the weapon of\\nknowledge of Your glory and attractiveness, which make the devotee fall in\\nlove (pr�ty-utp�daka) with You\". Uddhava's statement here that His\\naffection for the Da��rhas, V���is, Andhakas, and S�tvatas is m�y� and his\\nprayer that this affection be removed is a kind of self-delusion on\\nUddhava's part, for these kinsmen of his are all perfect liberated souls.\\n     In the words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 0 1.8.41 quoted here, Queen Kunt�\\nthinks: \"If Lord K���a departs from Hastin�pura, that will be inauspicious\\nfor the P���avas, and if He does not depart from Hastin�pura and return to\\nDv�rak� that will be inauspicious for the V���is. Her heart thus agitated\\nby competeing affections for these two sides of of her family, Queen Kunt�\\nhere prays that the affection she bears for her kinsmen be destroyed. The\\ntruth is that when she sees how the two sides of her family dearly love\\nLord K���a, her own love for Lord K���a increases. Therefore, the pretext\\nof saying {.sy 168}Please destroy my affection for my kinsmen\", Queen Kunt�\\nreally prays: \"Please do not leave the association of either of the two\\nsides of my family.\" After Queen Kunt� offered her prayers, Lord K���a\\nstill prepared to depart. �r�la S�ta Gosv�m� explains in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(1.8.45):\\n\\n\\nt�� b�dham ity up�mantrya. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"Thus accepting the prayers of Sr�mat� Kunt�dev�, the Lord\\nsubsequently informed other ladies of His departure by entering the palace\\nof Hastin�pura. But upon preparing to leave, He was stopped by King\\nYudhi��him, who implored Him lovingly.\"*.\\n\\n     In �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 11.29.39 Uddhava also prayed to attain Lord\\nK���a's association. �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 11.29.39-40 was spoken by Uddhava.\\n\\n"
