      "sourceStartLine": 8695,
      "content": "\\n\\n     The supremely blissful Supreme Personality of Godhead has two kinds of\\ninternal potency: 1. the potency of His linmitless qualities and opulences,\\nand 2. the internal potency that is His own body. This second potency is\\nmanifest only in His own transcendental body. The first potency is manifest\\noutside His body and is known by the name Goddess Lak�m�. The form of\\nGoddess Lak�m� is thus the origin of all qualities and opulences. Becuase\\nHe is always perfect and complete, the blissful Supreme Personality of\\nGodhead is not different from His qualities and opulences, and therefore\\nthese two opulences are not separate from each other. Also, the Lord is\\ncontrolled by the love His devotees bear for Him. This is certainly true in\\nrelation to oddess Lsk�m�, who loves Him dearly. It is said in �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (8.8.23):\\n\\n\\neva� vim��y�vyabhic�ri-sad-gu�air\\n     vara� nijaik��rayatay�gu���rayam\\nvavre vara� sarva-gu�air apek�ita�\\n     ram� mukunda� nirapek�am �psitam\\n\\n\\n     \"In this way, after full deliberation, the goddess of fortune accepted\\nMukunda as her husband because although He is independent and not in want\\nof her, He possesses all transcendental qualities and mystic powers and is\\ntherefore the most desirable.\"*\\n\\n     In this verse the words \"avyabhic�ri-sad-gu�ai�\" mean \"supreme with\\nqualities that have no defect\", {.sy 168}nijaik��rayatay�\" means \"without\\nbeing dependent on anyone\", and \"gu���rayam\" means \"He whose qualities are\\nperfect\". In this way the Lord's qualities are described. The words \"sarva-\\ngu�air apek�ita� nirapek�am �psitam\" mean \"because His nature is full of\\ntranscendental bliss, the Supreme Personality of Godhead has all good\\nqualities. Therefore Goddess Lak�m� chose Him.\" Thisverse was spoken by\\n�r�la �ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
