      "headingType": "anuccheda",
      "sourceStartLine": 9154,
      "content": "\\n\\n     That the Supreme Personality of Godhead is controlled by the love of\\nthe devotees in sakhya-rasa is described in these words of �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (1.16.16):\\n\\n\\ns�rathya-p�ra�ada-sevana-sakhya-dautya-\\n     v�r�san�nugamana-stavana-pra��m�n\\nsnigdhe�u p���u�u jagat-pra�ati� ca vi��or\\n     bhakti� karoti n�-pati� cara��ravinde\\n\\n\\n     \"Mah�r�ja Par�k�it heard that out of His causeless mercy Lord K���a\\n(Vi��u), who is universally obeyed, rendered all kinds of service to the\\nmalleable sons of P���u by accepting posts ranging from chariot driver to\\npresident to messenger, friend, night watchman, etc., according to the will\\nof the P���avas, obeying them like a servant and offering obeisances like\\none younger in years. When he heard this, Mah�r�ja Par�k�it became\\noverwhelmed with devotion to the lotus feet of the Lord.\"*\\n\\n     This verse means: \"Hearing that Lord Vi��u, who is universally obeyed,\\nhad rendered all kinds of service to the malleable sons of P���u, service\\nbeginning with becoming their chariot driver, Mah�r�ja Par�k�it became\\noverwhelmed with devotion to the lotus feet of the Lord.\" Here \"p�ra�adam\"\\nmeans \"acceptance of presidency in the assembly\", \"sevana\" means \"obeying\\nthe desires in the heart\", and \"v�r�sana\" means \"staying awake at night and\\nstanding guard with a sword in one's hand\". This verse was spoken by �r�la\\nS�ta Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
