      "content": "\\n\\n     That the Supreme Personality of Godhead is controlled by the love of\\nthe devotees in ���g�ra-rasa is described in these words of �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (10.32.22):\\n\\n\\nna p�raye 'ha� niravadya-sa�yuj��\\n     sva-s�dhu-k�tya� vibudh�yu��pi va�\\ny� m�bhajan durjara-geha-���khal�h\\n     sa�v��cya tad va� pratiy�tu s�dhun�\\n\\n\\n     \"I am not able to repay My debt for your spotless service, even within\\na lifetime of Brahm�. Your connection with Me is beyond reproach. You have\\nworshiped Me, cutting off all domestic ties, which are difficult to break.\\nTherefore please let your own glorious deeds be your compensation.\"*\\n\\n     In the verse the word \"niravadya\" means {.sy 168}pure because their\\nnature and actions are both opure\", {.sy 168}sa�yuj��\" menas \"contact with\\nthem\", \"va� sva-s�dhu-k�tya�\" means \"supremely blissful devotional service\\nto Me\", and \"na p�raye\" means \"I have not power to repay\". Someone may ask:\\n\"Why does the Lord have not power to repay the gop�s?\" The answer is given\\nin the words \"I could not repay you even within a lifetime of Brahm�.\" The\\nLord says: \"Your love for Me is so great that for My sake you disobeyed\\neven the rules of custom and religion.\" This the Lord said in the third and\\nfourth lines of this verse. There the Lord said: \"Please let your own\\nglorious deeds be your compensation. I am always in debt to you.\" This\\nverse was spoken by �r�la �ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
