      "content": "\\n\\n     Materialistic persons cannot understand this truth of the Lord. This\\nis described in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (1.11.37):\\n\\n\\ntam aya� manyate loko\\n     hy asa�gam api sa�ginam\\n�tmaupamyena manuja�\\n     vy�p��v�na� yato 'budha�\\n\\n\\n     \"The common materialistic conditioned souls speculate that the Lord is\\none of them. Out of their ignorance they think that the Lord is affected by\\nmatter, although He is unattached.\"*\\n\\n     Here the word \"ayam loka�\" means: \"the people in general\", \"asaktam\\napi\" means \"although not attached to the material modes of nature\", {.sy\\n168}�tmaupamyena manuja� vy�p��v�na� manyate\" means {.sy 168}they think the\\nLord isa lusty material man like themselves\", and \"yato 'budha�\" means\\n\"they think in this way because they are not intelligent\".\\n\\n"
