      "sourceLabel": "Anuccheda 139",
      "headingType": "anuccheda",
      "sourceStartLine": 9936,
      "content": "\\n\\n     Here someone may ask: \"Do the Lord's consorts know the Lord possesses\\nthis great opulence of detachment? If they know, then their loev for Him in\\ntheir confidential pastimes with Him would certainly be broken into\\npieces.\" Fearing that someone might spoeak these words, the author of\\n�r�mad-Bh�gavatam explains (�r�mad-Bh�gavatam 1.11.39):\\n\\n\\nta� menire 'bal� mau�hy�t\\n     strai�a� c�nuvrata� rahah\\napram��a-vido bhartur\\n     ��vara� matayo yath�\\n\\n\\n     \"The simple and delicate women truly thought that Lord �r� K���a,\\ntheir beloved husband, followed them and was dominated by them. They were\\nunaware of the extent of the glories of their husband, as the atheists are\\nunaware of Him as the supreme controller.\"*\\n\\n     Here the word \"��vara�\" means \"even though He is the Supreme\\nPersonality of Godhead\", \"raha�\" means in confidential pastimes\",\\n\"mau�hy�t\" means {.sy 168}bewildered by love for Him\", \"apram��a-vido\\nbhartu�\" means \"unaware of their husband's true opulences and powers\",\\n\"strai�a� c�nuvrata� menire\" means \"they thought He weas controlled by\\nwomen, a follower of women\". This idea they have is not the truth. Here the\\nwords \"matayo yath�\" mean \"this idea was created by the desire born of\\ntheir love for Him\". The Supreme Lord appears before His devotees in the\\nway they desire Him to appear. This is confirmed by the Lord HImself in\\nthese words of Bhagavad-g�t� (4.11):\\n\\n\\nye yath� m�m. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"All of them, as they surrender unto Me, I reward accordingly.\"*\\n\\n     This is also confirmed by the following words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(10.14.2):\\n\\n\\nsveccha-mayasya. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"O Lord, Your appearance as a cowherd child is for the benefit of the\\ndevotees, to fulfill their desires.\"\\n\\n     �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 1.11.39 quoted in this anuccheda was spoken by �r�la\\nS�ta Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
