      "headingType": "anuccheda",
      "sourceStartLine": 9988,
      "content": "\\n\\n     That the Lord's consorts did not understand the truth about their\\nhusband is confirmed by the following words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.61.2):\\n\\n\\n\\ng�h�d anapaga� v�k�ya\\n     r�ja-putryo 'cyutam sthitam\\npre��ha� nyama�sata sva� sva�\\n     na tat-tattva-vida� striya�\\n\\n\\n     \"Because each of these princesses saw that Lord Acyuta never left her\\npalace, each thought herself the Lord's favorite. These women did not\\nunderstand the truth about Him.\"***\\n\\n     Here the words \"pre��ha� nyama�sata sva� sva�\" mean \"each one thought\\nherself the most dear\", and \"na tat-tattva-vida�\" means \"each one thinking\\nherself the most dear, they did not understand the truth.\"\\n\\n"
