      "content": "\\n\\n     The charms of the Lord's wives are described in these words of �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (10.61.4):\\n\\n\\nsm�y�valoka-lava-dar�ita-bh�va-h�ri-\\n     bhr�-ma��ala-prahita-saurata-mantra-�au��ai�\\npatnyas tu �o�a�a-sahasram ana�ga-b��air\\n     yasyendriya� vimathitu� kara�air na �eku�\\n\\n\\n     \"The arched eyebrows of these sixteen-thousand queens enchantingly\\nexpressed those ladies' secret intentions through coyly smiling sidelong\\nglances. Thus their eyebrows boldly set forth conjugal messages. Yet even\\nwith these arrows of Cupid, and with other means as well, they could not\\nagitate Lord K���a's senses.\"***\\n\\n     Even with flirting arrows of Cupid they could not agitate the Lord.\\nHere the word \"sm�ya\" means \"smiling\", \"bh�va\" means \"intention\", \"bhr�-\\nma��ala-prahita\" means \"sent from the eyebrows\", {.sy 168}saurata-mantra\"\\nmeans \"mantras of love\", and {.sy 168}�au��ai�\" means \"bold\". This verse\\nwas spoken by �r�la �ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
