      "headingType": "anuccheda",
      "sourceStartLine": 10314,
      "content": "\\n\\n     If He does not wish to be bewildered, the Supreme Personality of\\nGodhead will not be bewildered. This is seen in the description of the\\nmagical powers of the demon ��lva in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(10.77.30-31):\\n\\n\\neva� vadanti r�jar�e\\n     ��aya� ke ca n�nvit��\\n\\nkva �oka-mohau sneho v�\\n     bhaya� v� ye 'j�a-sambhav��\\nkva c�kha��ita-vij��na-\\n     j��nai�varya� tv akha��ita�. . .\\n\\n\\n    \"Such ios the account given by some sages, O wise king, but those who\\nspeak in this illogical way are contradicting themselves, having forgotten\\ntheir own previous statements.***\\n     \"How can lamentations, bewilderment, material affection, or fear, all\\nborn out of ignorance, be ascibed to the infinte Supreme Lordeee, whose\\nperception, knowledge, and power are all similarly infinite?\" ***\\n\\n     This verse askes: \"How can lamentation and other like qualities, which\\nare all born from ignorance, be manifest in the Supreme Lord?\".This verse\\nwas spoken by �r�la �ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
