      "sourceLabel": "Anuccheda 145",
      "headingType": "anuccheda",
      "sourceStartLine": 10344,
      "content": "\\n\\n     When the Lord does manifest lamentation or other like emotions it is\\nbecause He is controlled by the love of His devotee. An examples is seen in\\nthis description of Lord R�macandra's pastimes in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(9.11.16):\\n\\n\\ntac chrutv� bhagav�n r�ma�. . .\\n\\n\\n    \"After hearing the news of Mother S�t�'s entering the earth, the\\nSupreme Personality of Godhead was certainly aggrieved. ASlthough He is the\\nSupreme Personality of Godhead, upon remembering the exalted qualities of\\nMother S�t�, He could not check His grief in transcendental love.\"*\\n\\n     Another example is seen in this description of the Lord's pastimes\\nwith Sud�m� br�hma�a in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.80.19):\\n\\n\\nsakhyu� priyasya viprar�e�. . .\\n\\n\\n    \" The lotus-eyed Supreme Lord felt intense ecstasy upon touching the\\nbody of His dear friend, the wise br�hma�a, and thus He shed tears of\\nlove.\"***\\n\\n     Another example is seen in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (1.8.31):\\n\\n\\ngopy �dade tvayi krt�gasi d�ma t�vad\\n     y� te da���ru-kalil�njana-sambhram�k�am\\nvaktra� nin�ya bhaya-bh�vanay� sthitasya\\n     s� m�� vimohayati bhir api yad bibheti\\n\\n\\n     \"My dear K���a, Ya�od� took up a rope to bind You when You committed\\nan offense, and Your perturbed eyes overflooded with tears, which washed\\nthe mascara from Your eyes. And You were afraid, though fear personified is\\nafraid of You. This sight is bewildering to me.\"*\\n\\n     Here it is said that fear personified is afraid of the Lord. In this\\nway the Lord has all glory, power, opulence, and knowledge. He is never\\ntruly afraid. In the same way He is never truly bewildered. Even so, in\\nthis pastime fear entered His heart (bhaya-bh�vanay� sthitasya). This verse\\nwas spoken by Queren Kunt� to the Supreme Personality of Godhead.\\n\\n"
