      "headingType": "anuccheda",
      "sourceStartLine": 10961,
      "content": "\\n\\n     These truths of the Supreme Lord's pastimes, truths discussed in the\\nprevious explanations given here, are confirmed by these words of �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (10.33.19):\\n\\n\\nk�tv� t�vantam �tm�na�\\n     y�vat�r gopa-yo�ita�\\nreme sa bhagav��s t�bhir\\n     �tm�r�mo 'pi l�lay�\\n\\n\\n     \"Expanding Himself as many times as there were cowherd women to\\nassociate with, the Supreme Lord, though self-satisfied, playfully enjoyed\\ntheir company.\"***\\n\\n     Here the words \"rar�ma �bhi�\" mean \"the lOrd enjoyed pastimes with the\\ngop�s\". It is said in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (3.15.43):\\n\\n\\ntasy�ravinda-nayanasya. . . cak�ra te��� sa�k�obham ak�ara ju��m api citta-\\ntanvo�\\n\\n\\n     \"When the breeze carrying the aroma of tulas� leaves from the toes of\\nthe lotus feet of the Personality of Godhead entered the nostrils of those\\nsages, they experienced a change both in body and in mind, even though they\\nwere attached to the impersonal Brahman understanding.\"*\\n\\n     �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 10.33.19 means: \"When the Lord desired to enjoy\\npastimes with all the the gop�s simultaneously, His pastime potency\\narranged that the Lord be manifested in this way.\" The word \"lilaya\" in\\nthis verse indicates that this pastimes was arranged by the Lord's pastime\\npotency. The Lord did not make these arrangements Himself. Here the words\\n{.sy 168}k�tv� t�vantam �tm�nam\" indicate that the Lord manifested His own\\nform as many times as there were gop�s. This verse was spoken by �r�la\\n�ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
