      "content": "\\n\\n     The Lord's pastimes of detachment from the material world are\\nconsidered sweet by the neophyte devotees. These pastimes are described in\\nthese words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (3.3.22):\\n\\n\\ntasyaiva� ramam��asya\\n     samvatsara-ga��n bah�n\\ng�hame�he�u yoge�u\\n     vir�ga� samaj�yata\\n\\n\\n    \"The Lord was thus engaged in household life for many, many years, but\\nat last His detachment from ephemeral sex life wa fully manifested.\"*\\n\\n     Here the world \"g�hame�he�u\" means in the religious duties of pious\\nhousehold life\", and {.sy 168}vir�ga�\" means \"detachment\". This verse was\\nspoken by �r�m�n Uddhava to Vidura.\\n\\n"
