      "content": "\\n\\n     Now will be considered the various objects (dravya) included amongst\\nthe udd�panas (impetuses for ecstatic love). Included amongst these objects\\nare the Lord's ornaments, musical instruemnts, places, markings, personal\\nassociates, devotees, tulas�, remnants, and many other things. The Lord's\\nornaments include His garments, ornaments, flower-ornaments, and many other\\nthings. All these are manifested on the Lord transcendental form. They were\\ndescribed in the Bhagavat-sandarbha, Anuccheda 61. They are described in\\nthese words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (3.2.12):\\n\\n\\nbh��a�a-bh��a���gam\\n\\n\\n    \"His (�r� K���a's) transcendental body is the ornament of all\\nornaments.\"*\\n\\n     This is means that is because they come into contact with Lord K���a's\\nhandsomeness, bodily fragrance, and other glorious features that the Lord's\\nornaments have the power to decorate the Lord's transcendental body. On\\ntheir own the ornaments have no power to decorate the Lord's body. Because\\nthey are in contact with the Lord's form, potencies, pastimes, and\\nqualities, the Lord's ornaments become glorious. They are described in\\nthese words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.32.2):\\n\\n\\np�t�mbara-dhara� sragv�\\n     sak��n manmatha-manmatha�\\n\\n\\n     \"Then Lord K���a, a smile on His lotus face, appeared before the\\ngop�s. Wearing a garland and a yellow garment, He directly appeared as one\\nwho can bewilder the mind of Cupid, who himself bewilders the minds of\\nordinary people.\"***\\n\\n     In this way it is said that the flower-garland and yellow garments\\ndecorate the the Supreme Lord, whose glorious handsomeness has no equal or\\nsuperior. It is also said in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.41.35):\\n\\n\\n�d���ny eva v�s��si\\n     nitya� giri-vane-car��\\n\\n\\n    \"You impudent boys! You're accustomed to roaming the mountains and\\nforests, and yet You would dare put on such closhes as these! These are the\\nking's possessions You're asking for!\"***\\n\\n     These words were spoken by a demonic washerman. He saw the lord's\\nclothing and ornaments in that way. The way the people in general saw the\\nLord's clothing and ornaments is described in these words of Vi��u Pur��a:\\n\\n\\nsuvar���jana-c�r��bhy��\\n     tau tad� bh��it�mbarau\\n\\n\\n     \"K���a and Balar�ma were decorated with fragrant ointments and\\npowders, with splendid garments, and with golden ornaments.\"\\n\\n     The Lord's ornaments are also described in these words of �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (10.23.22):\\n\\n\\n�y�ma� hira�ya-paridhim. . .\\n\\n\\n    \"His complexion was dark blue and His garment golden. Wearing a peacock\\nfeather, colored minerals, sprigs of flower buds, and a garland of forest\\nflowers and leaves, he was dressed just like a dramatic dancer. He rested\\none hand upon the shoulder of a friend and with the other twirled a lotus.\\nLiles graced His ears, His hair hung down over His cheeks, and His\\nlotuslike face was smiling.\"***\\n\\n     Kaliya-, Varuna, and Indra who offered abhiskeato the Lord, all\\npresented to thee Loerd gifts of glorious garments and ornaments. By the\\narrangement of the Lord's internal potency Lord K���a accepted the\\ngarmanets that had belonged to Ka�sa. Also by the arrangement of the Lord's\\ninternal potency Lord K���a accepted the many wives of Narak�sura. The\\nLord's weapons include His clud and cakra. His musical instruments include\\nHis flute and conchshell. His places include V�nd�vana ande Mathur�. His\\nauspicious markings include the markings on the soles of His feet. His\\npersonal associates include the cowherd people and the Y�davas. The\\nremnants of things He has used include gop�-candana. Amongst the udd�panas\\nare also the times sacred to the Lord, times such as Janm���am�. All these\\nare udd�panas that arouse the devotees' love for the Supreme Personality of\\nGodhead. An example of the udd�panas arousing a devotee's attraction for\\nthe Lord is seen in these owrds of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.42.9):\\n\\n\\ntato r�pa-gu�aud�rya-\\n     sampann� pr�ha ke�avam\\nuttar�y�ntam �k��ya\\n     smayant� j�ta-h�c-chay�\\n\\n\\n    \"Now endowed with beauty, character, and generosity, Trivakr� began to\\nfeel lusty desires for Lored Ke�ava. Taking hold of the upper end of His\\ncloth, she smiled and addressed Him as follows.\"***\\n\\n     The meaning of this verse is clear. This verse was spoken by �r�la\\n�ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
