      "sourceStartLine": 12735,
      "content": "\\n\\n     Now we will consider the v�tsalya-rasa enjoyed by the Lord's father,\\nMah�r�ja Vasudeva, and by others also, and which is sometimes properly\\nmanifested, and sometimes improperly manifested in the form of ras�bh�sa.\\nV�salya-rasa is seen in these words spoken by Mah�r�ja Nanda (�r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam 10.47.66):\\n\\n\\nmanaso v�ttayo na� syu�. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"May our thoughts always take shelter of K���a's lotus feet, may our\\nwords always chant His names, and may our bodies always bow down to Him and\\nserve Him.\"*\\n\\n     Lord K���a's spiritual master also has a relationship in v�tsalya-\\nrasa. This is seen in these words spoken by Sud�m� br�hma�a in �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (10.80.44):\\n\\n\\nkim asm�bhir anirv�tta�\\n     deva-deva jagad-guro\\nbhavat� satya-k�mena\\n     ye��� v�so guror abh�t\\n\\n\\n     \"What could I possibly have failed to achieve, O Lord of lords, O\\nuniversal teacher, since I was able to personally live with You, whose\\nevery desire is fulfilled, at the home of our spiritual master?\"***\\n\\n     V�tsalya-rasa is also seen in these words of Sr�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(10.80.6 and 27):\\n\\n\\nk���asy�s�t sakh� ka�cit. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"Lord K���a had a certain br�hma�a friend (named Sud�m�) who was most\\nlearned in Vedic knowledge and detached from all sense enjoyment.\\nFurthermore, his mind was peaceful and his senses subdued.\"***\\n\\n\\nkathay�� cakratu�. . .karau g�hya parasparam\\n\\n\\n     \"Taking each other's hands, O King, K���a and Sud�m� talked pleasantly\\nabout how they once lived together in the school of their guru.\"***\\n\\n     In this way v�tsalya-rasa is described. �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 10.80.44\\nquoted in this anuccheda was spoken by �r�la �ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
