      "headingType": "anuccheda",
      "sourceStartLine": 12789,
      "content": "\\n\\n     ���g�ra-rasa is seen in the following words spoken by Queen Rukmi�� in\\n�r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.60.39):\\n\\n\\ntvam nyasta-da��a-munibhir gadit�nubh�va\\n     �tm�tma-da� ca jagat�m iti me v�to 'si. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"Knowing that the great sages who have renounced the sannyasi's danda\\nproclaim Your glories, that You are the Supreme Soul of all the worlds, and\\nthat You are so gracious that You give away even Your own self, I chose You\\nas my husband, rejecting Lord Brahm�, Lord �iva, and the rulers of heaven,\\nwhose aspirations are all frustrated by the force of time, which is born\\nfrom Your eyebrows. What interest, then, could I have in any other\\nsuitors?\"***\\n\\n     In this verse the word \"�tm�\" means {.sy 168}param�tm�\", and \"�tma-\\nda�\" means \"who reveals Himself to the liberated souls\". Someone may say\\nthat in this vesre the mixture of ���g�ra-rasa and ��nta-rasa creat\\nras�bh�sa. This is not so. What seems to be santa-rasa here is simply\\ndevotional service, is Queen Rukmi��'s declaration that she is the\\nmaidservant ofher dear husband. Her words are appropriate because they show\\nthat she is the crest jewel of all faithful wives devoted to their\\nhsubands. Although they eacvh had hundreds of maidservants, Lord K���a's\\nqueens considered themselves the maidservants of Lord K���a. This is\\ndescribed in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.59.45):\\n\\n\\nd�s�-�at� api vibhor vidadhu� sma d�syam\\n\\n\\n     \"Although the Supreme Lord's queens each had hundreds of maidservants,\\nthey chose to personally serve the Lord..\"***\\n\\n     Queen Rukmi�� is Goddess Lak�m� herself. Her devotion to the Lord is\\nmixed with knowledge of the Lord's supreme power and opulence. Therefore\\nthere is no ras�b�asa is her prayers describing that opulence. �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam 10.6.39 quoted in this anuccheda was spoken by Queen Rukmi��.\\n\\n"
