      "content": "\\n\\n     It is said in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.42.10):\\n\\n\\nehi v�ra g�ha� y�mo\\n     na tv�� tyaktum ihotsahe\\ntvayonmathita-citt�y��\\n     pras�da purusar�abha\\n\\n\\n     \"Come, O hero. Let us go to my house. I cannot bear to leave You here.\\nO best of males, please take pity on me, since You ahve agitated my\\nmind.\"***\\n\\n     Someone may say that it is not appropriate for a heroine to be very\\nagitated, and therefore this verse presents an �bh�sa in ���g�ra-rasa. The\\ntruth is there is nothing incmpatible in this verse, for even in ordinary\\naffairs this kind of agitation is not inappropriate. This verse was spoken\\nby Kubj� to the Supreme Personality of Godhead.\\n\\n"
