      "sourceLabel": "Anuccheda 197",
      "headingType": "anuccheda",
      "sourceStartLine": 13838,
      "content": "\\n\\n     To confirm what was said before, the following two verses of �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam declare that devotion to the Lord is the only way one can attain\\nthe Lord's mercy, mercy that is the sweetest of the Lord's virtues. This is\\nconfirmed by the following words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (5.19.7):\\n\\n\\nna janma n�na� mahato na saubhaga�\\n     na v�� na buddhir n�k�tis to�a-hetu�\\ntair yad vis����n api no vanaukasa�\\n     cak�ra sakhye bata lak�man�graja�\\n\\n\\n     \"One cannot establish a friendship with the Supreme Lord R�macandra on\\nthe basis of material qualities such as one's birth in an aristocratic\\nfamily, one's personal beauty, one's eloquence, one's sharp intelligence or\\none's superior race or nation. None of these qualifications is actually a\\nprerequisite for friendship with Lord �r� R�macandra. Otherwise how is it\\npossible that although we un- civilized inhabitants of the forest have not\\ntaken noble births, although we have no physical beauty and although we\\ncannot speak like gentlemen, Lord R�macandra has nevertheless accepted us\\nas friends?\"*\\n\\n     In this verse the word \"janma mahata�\" means {.sy 168}birth from the\\nSupreme Personality of Godhead\", {.sy 168}saubhagam\" means \"beauty\",\\n\"�k�ti�\" means \"birth\", \"yat\" means \"from which\", {.sy 168}tai�\" means\\n\"birth and other like things\", {.sy 168}vis����n\" means \"rejected\", \"na�\"\\nmeans {.sy 168}we who pleased the Lord with our devotional service of\\nsearching for Sita-devi and engaging in other kinds of devotional service\\nalso\", \"bata\" means indeed\", {.sy 168}lak�man�graja�\" the elder brother of\\nLak�ma�a, who is endowed with all virtues and who is Sumitr�'s son\", {.sy\\n168}sakhye\" means \"made friendship, for in these pastimes friendship and\\nnot servitude was the appropriate rasa\". This verse describes Sugr�va.\\n\\n\\nAnucchedab 198\\n\\n\\n     The next verse declares (�r�mad-Bh�gavatam 5.19.8):\\n\\n\\nsuro 'suro v�py atha v�naro narah\\n     sarv�tman� ya� suk�taj�am uttamam\\nbhajeta r�ma� manuj�k�ti� hari�\\n     ya uttar�n anayat kosal�n divam iti\\n\\n\\n     \"Therefore, whether one is a demigod or a demon, a man or a creature\\nother than man, such as a beast or bird, everyone should worship Lord\\nR�macandra, the Supreme Personality of Godhead, who appears on this earth\\njust like a human being. There is no need of great austerities or penances\\nto worship the Lord, for Me accepts even a small service offered by His\\ndevotee. Thus He is satisfied, and as soon as He is satisfied, the devotee\\nis successful. Indeed, Lord �r� R�macandra brought all the devotees of\\nAyodhy� back home, back to Godhead [Vaiku��ha].\"*\\n\\n     The previous verse described devotion to the Lord's humanlike\\ntranscendental form, devotion based on knowledge of the Lord's true nature\\nand status. This verse describes devotion based on perception of the Lord's\\nsweetness. In that situation the devotee worships the humanlike form of the\\nLord (manuj�k�ti� harim). Here the word \"r��am\" means \"the form of Lord\\nR�ma, not the form of Kapila or any other form of the Lord\". Here \"uttamam\"\\nmeans \"whose transcendental qualities have no equal ro superior\", and\\n\"suk�taj{.sy 241}am\" means \"He who is pleased by even a small quantity of\\ndevotional service\". This verse was spoken by �r� Hanum�n.\\n\\n"
