      "sourceLabel": "Anuccheda 200",
      "headingType": "anuccheda",
      "sourceStartLine": 13988,
      "content": "\\n\\n     As before, an example of what seems to be ras�bh�sa of a primary and\\nsecondary rasa, but in the end is understood to be a compatible mixture of\\nrasas is seen in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.16.20):\\n\\n\\ngopyo 'nurakta-manaso bhagavaty anante\\n     tat-sauh�da-smita-viloka-gira� smarantya�\\ngraste 'hin� priyatame bh��a-du�kha-tapt��\\n     ��nya� priya-vyatih�ta� dad��us tri-lokam\\n\\n\\n     \"When the young gop�s, whose minds were constantly attached to K���a,\\nthe unlimited Supreme Lord, saw that He was now within the grips of the\\nserpent, they remembered His loving friendship, His smiling glances and His\\ntalks with them. Burning with great sorrow, they saw the entire universe as\\nvoid.\"***\\n\\n     Here the secondary rasa, karu�a-rasa (lamentation), is compatible, and\\nthe primary rasa, ���g�ra-rasa, seems to be incompatible. However, in this\\nsituation the gop�s' remembrace of Lord K���a's smiling glances acts to\\nmake their sorrow glorious. For this reason the mixture of these rasas is\\ncompatible, and there is no ras�bh�sa. This verse was spoken by �r�la\\n�ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
    },
