      "sourceStartLine": 14316,
      "content": "\\n\\n     A�raya-rasa is of two kinds: 1. ��raya-rasa in separation from the\\nLord, and 2. ��raya-rasa in direct association with the Lord. A�raya-rasa\\nin separation from the Lord is again of two kinds: 1. initial separation,\\nbefore meeting the Lord, and 2. separation when the Lord is far away.\\nA�raya-rasa in direct association with the Lord is also of two kinds: 1.\\neventually meeting the Lord again after one of the two kinds of separation,\\nand 2. the regular direct association called by the names {.sy 168}siddhi\"\\n(perfection\" and \"tu��i\" (happiness). Initial separation, before meeting\\nthe Lord, is described in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.70.31):\\n\\n\\niti m�gadha-samruddh�\\n     bhavad-dar�ana-ka�k�i�a�\\nprapann�� p�da-m�la� te\\n     d�n�n�� �a� vidh�yatam\\n\\n\\n     \"This is the message of the kings imprisoned by Jar�sandha, who all\\nhanker for Your audience, having surrendered to Your feet. Please bestow\\ngood fortune on these poor souls.\"***\\n\\n     Here the words \"bhavad-dar�ana-ka�k�i�a�\" indicate that the kings\\nyearned to become free of their imprisonment in order to see Lord K���a. In\\nthis is seen the sth�yi-bh�va. Here the soles of the Lord's feet (p�da-\\nm�lam) are the �lambana, the kings' imprisonment is the udd�pana, their\\nsurrender to the Lord is the udbh�svara, their eagerness and humility are\\nthe sa�c�ri-bh�vas. From this the s�ttvika-bh�vas and other bh�vas are\\nknown. This verse was spoken by the kings' messenger to the Supreme\\nPersonality of Godhead.\\n\\n"
