      "content": "\\n\\n     In the Eleventh Canto is a description of S�mba's acting in an\\nimproper way (by teasing N�rada Muni). It should be understood that those\\nactions  were instigated by Lord K���a Himself by His own wish to arrange\\nfor certain pastimes. Amongst all of Lord K���a's sons, �r� Rukmi��'s ans\\nwere the best. This is described in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(10.61.9):\\n\\n\\npradyumna-pramukh� j�t�\\n     rukmi�y�� n�vam�� pitu�\\n\\n\\n     \"Rukmi��'s sons, headed by Pradyumna, were not less than their\\nfather.\"\\n\\n     Again and again the superiority of those sons is described. This verse\\nwas spoken by �r�la �ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
