      "content": "\\n\\n     Even when he is in distress, a devotee in v�tsalya-rasa may pretend to\\nsmile in order to reassure Lord K���a. An example of this is seen in the\\nfollowing words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.11.6):\\n\\n\\nul�khala� vikar�anta�\\n     d�mn� baddha� svam �tmajam\\nvilokya nanda� prahasad-\\n     vadano vimumoca ha\\n\\n\\n     \"When Nanda Mah�r�ja saw his own son bound with ropes to the wooden\\nmortar and dragging it, he smiled and released K���a from His bonds.\"*\\n\\n     An alternate reading here is \"prahasad-vadanam\" (Lord K���a weas\\nsmiling). This verse was spoken by  �r�la �ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
