      "sourceStartLine": 16417,
      "content": "\\n\\n     After the devotees attain Lord K���a's direct association the\\necstasies of v�tsalya-rasa become perfectly manifest. They are seen in\\nthese words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.5.12):\\n\\n\\nta ��i�a�. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"Offering blessings to the newborn child, K���a, the wives and the\\ndaughters of the cowherd men said, `May You become the king of Vraja and\\nlogn maintain all its inhabitants.' They sprinkled a mixture of turmeric\\npowder, oil, and water upon the birthless Supreme Lord and offered their\\nprayers.\"*\\n\\n     When the devotees become separated from Lord K���a, the ecstasies of\\nv�tsalya-rasa are also seen. An example is given in these words of �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (10.46.27-28):\\n\\n\\niti sa�sm�tya sa�sm�tya\\n     nanda� k����nurakta-dh��\\naty-utka��ho 'bhavat t�����\\n     prema-prasara-vihvala�\\n\\n\\n     \"Thus intensely remembering K���a again and again, Nanda Mah�r�ja, his\\nmind completely attached to the Lord, felt extreme anxiety and fell silent,\\novercome by the strength of his love.***\\n\\n\\nya�od� var�yam�n�ni\\n     putrasya carit�ni ca\\n���vaty a�runi av�sr�k��t\\n     sneha-snuta-payodhar�\\n\\n\\n     \"As mother Ya�od� heard the descriptions of her son's activities, she\\npoured out her tears, and milk flowed from her breasts out of love.\"***\\n\\n     The meaning of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 10.46.27-28 is clear. These verses\\nwere spoken by �r�la �ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n\\nAnucchedas 247 and 248\\n\\n\\n     After being separated from Him, when they again meet K���a, the\\ndevotees in v�tsalya-rasa are very pleased. This is seen in the following\\nwords of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.82.35):\\n\\n\\nt�v �tm�sanam �ropya\\n\\n\\n     \"Raising their two sons onto their laps and holding Them in their\\narms, Nanda and saintly mother Ya�od� forgot their sorrow.\"***\\n\\n     These ecstasies are also seen in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(10.84.66):\\n\\n\\nnandas tu sakhyu� priya-k�t\\n     prem�� govinda-r�mayo�\\nadya sva iti m�s��s tr�n\\n     yadubhir m�nito 'vasat\\n\\n\\n     \"And on his part, Nanda was also full of affection for his friend\\nVasudeva. Thus during the following days Nanda would repeatedly announce,\\n`I will be leaving later today' and `I will be leaving tomorrow'. But out\\nof love for K���a and Balar�ma he remained there for three more months,\\nhonored by all the Yadus.\"***\\n\\n     In this verse it is said: \"But out of love for K���a and Balar�ma he\\nremained there for three more months.\" For three months he would repeatedly\\nannounce, `I will be leaving later today' and `I will be leaving\\ntomorrow'.\" Overcome with bliss, Nanda felt those three months apss as if\\nthey were only two days. Someone may ask: \"What did he do as he resided\\nthere?\" The answer is given here in the words: \"Nanda was also full of\\naffection for his friend Vasudeva.\" This means that when Vasudeva was\\npresent Nanda did not act as if K���a were his son. Neither did he attempt\\nto take K���a back with him to Vraja. Then it is said here: \"Nanda was\\nhonored by all the Yadus.\" Afterward Nanda was again separated from Lord\\nK���a. This is described in the following words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(10.84.67-69):\\n\\n\\ntata� k�mai� p�ryam�na�\\n     sa-vraja� saha-bandhava�\\npar�rdhy�bhara�a-k�auma-\\n     n�n�narghya-paricchadai�\\n\\nvasudevograsenabhy��\\n     k���oddhava-bal�dibhi�\\ndattam �d�ya paribarha�\\n     y�pito yadubhir yayau\\n\\n\\n     \"Then, after Vasudeva, Ugrasena, K���a, Uddhava, Balar�ma, and others\\nhad fulfilled his desires and presented him with precious ornaments, fine\\nlinen, and varieties of priceless household furnishing, Nanda Mah�r�ja\\naccepted all these gifts and took his leave. Seen off by all the Yadus, he\\ndeparted with his family members and the residents of Vraja.***\\n\\n\\nnando gopas ca gopya� ca\\n     govinda-cara��mbuje\\nmana� k�ipta� punar hartum\\n     an��� mathur�� yayau\\n\\n\\n     \"Unable to withdraw their minds from Lord Govinda's lotus feet, where\\nthey had surrendered them, Nanda and the cowherd men and women returned to\\nMathur�.\"***\\n\\n     In �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 10.84.67 the word \"k�mai�\" means \"with the\\ndesires that begin with the desire that K���a would return to Vraja\", and\\nthe word \"p�ryam�na�\" means \"satisfied by Lord K���a\". It was Lord Balar�ma\\nwho returned to Vraja. In describing that pastime �r�la �ukadeva Gosv�m�\\nsaid in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.65.6):\\n\\n\\nk���e kamala-patr�k�e\\n     sanyast�khila-r�dhasa�\\n\\n\\n     \"The cowherds had dedicated everything to lotus-eyed K���a.\"***\\n\\n     �r�la �r�dhara Sv�m� comments:\\n\\n     \"In this verse the word `k���e' means `for the purpose of attaining\\nLord K���a's association', and `     sanyast�khila-r�dhasa�' means `they\\nrenounced everything'.\"\\n\\n     In �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 10.84.67-69 it is said: {.sy 168}With great love\\nVasudeva and the others gave gifts of many ornaments.\" Here the word\\n\"�pita�\" means {.sy 168}escorted by a great army\". �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n10.84.69 describes the great love the people of Vraja felt for Lord K���a.\\nWhent hey had returned to Mathur�, the cowherd people again yearned for\\nLord K���a's association. �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 10.84.66-69 was spoken by �r�la\\n�ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
