      "content": "\\n\\n     The Supreme Lord's ordinary lovers (s�m�nya-vallabh�) include the girl\\nKubj� and the damsels on Mount Kail�sa, damsels described in the K�rma\\nPur��a. Kubj� is described in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.48.8):\\n\\n\\nsaiva� kaivalya-n�tha� ta�\\n     pr�pya du�pr�pyam ��varam\\na�ga-r�g�rpa�en�ho\\n     durbhagedam �yacata\\n\\n\\n     \"Having thus gotten the hard-to-get Supreme Lord by the simple act of\\noffering Him body ointment, unfortunate Trivakr� submitted to that Lord of\\nfreedom the following request.\"***\\n\\n     This verse says: \"Even though she was unfortuante, Kubj� attained the\\nSupreme Personality of Godhead simply by offering bodily ointment to Him.\\nThis is very surprising.\" Then Kubj� said to Lord K���a in �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (10.48.9):\\n\\n\\nsaho�yat�m. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"O beloved, please stay here with me for a few days more and enjoy. I\\ncannot bear to give up Your association, O lotus-eyed one.\"***\\n\\n     In �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 10.48.8 the word \"ay�cata\" means \"she approached\\nto beg a favor\". What were the characteristics of Lord K���a? It is said\\nhere that He is {.sy 168}kaivalya-n�tha\", which means \"the beloved whose\\nlove is pure\". Although originally she approached Lord K���a so that she\\nherself would find pleasure, at the end Kubj� loved K���a with pure and\\nselfless love. In this way she became like the goddesslike gop�s of Vraja.\\n�r� Rukmi�� and the other queens of Lord K���a are praised in these words\\nof �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.90.27):\\n\\n\\nya� sampary�caran prem��\\n     pada-samv�han�dibhi�\\njagad-guru� bhart�-buddhy�\\n     t�s�� ki� var�yate tapa�\\n\\n\\n     \"And how could one possibly describe the great austerities that had\\nbeen performed by the women who perfectly served Him, the spiritual master\\nof the universe, in pure ecstatic love? Thinking of Him as their husband,\\nthey rendered such intimate services as massaging His feet.\"***\\n\\n     The meaning of this verse is clear. This verse was spoken by �r�la\\n�ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
