      "sourceStartLine": 17863,
      "content": "\\n\\n     In addition to Lord K���a's queens (svak�ya), there are the\\ngoddesslike gop�s of Vraja, who love Lord K���a as their paramour\\n(parak�ya). No lovers are equal or superior to the gop�s, who are glorified\\nin these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.47.60):\\n\\n\\nn�ya� �riyo '�ga u nit�nta-rate� pras�da�\\n     sv�r-yo�it�� nalina-gandha-ruca� kuto 'ny��\\nr�sotasave 'sya bhuja-da��a-g�hi�a-ka��ha-\\n     labdh��i�a� ya udag�d vraja-vallabh�n�m\\n\\n\\n     \"When Lord �r� K���a was dancing with the gop�s in the r�sa-l�l�, the\\ngop�s were embraced by the arms of the Lord. This transcendental favor was\\nnever bestowed upon the goddess of fortune or other consorts in the\\nspiritual world. Indeed, never was such a thing even imagined by the most\\nbeautiful girls in the heavenly planets, whose bodily luster and aroma\\nresemble the lotus flower. Ansd what to speak of worldly women who are very\\nbeautiful according to material estimation?\"*\\n\\n     The gop�s are again glorified in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(10.44.14):\\n\\n\\ngopyas tapa� kim acaran yad amu�ya r�pa�. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"What austerities must the gop�s have performed! With their eyes they\\nalways drink the nectar of Lord K���a's form, which is the essence of\\nloveliness and is not to be equaled or surpassed. That lovliness is the\\nonly abode of beauty, fame, and opulence. It is self-perfect, ever fresh\\nand extremely rare.\"*\\n\\n     This verse says: \"The gop�s gazed at Lord K���a's form, which is not\\nto be equaled or surpassed\". The gop�s are again glorified in these words\\nof �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.44.15):\\n\\n\\ny� dohane 'vahanane mathanopalepa. . .\\n     . . .dhany� vraja-striya urukrama-citta-y�n��\\n\\n\\n     \"The ladies of Vraja are the most fortunate of women because, with\\ntheir minds fully attached to K���a and their throats always choked up with\\ntears, they constantly sing about Him while milking the cows, winnowing\\ngrain, churning butter, gathering cow dung for fuel, riding on swings,\\ntaking care of their crying babies, sprinkling the ground with water,\\ncleaning their houses, and so on. By their exalted K���a consciousness they\\nautomatically acquire all desirable things.\"***\\n\\n     In this verse the word \"urukrama-citta-y�n��\" means \"they whose\\nchariot is the all-powerful mind\". This means that wherever their minds\\nwent, they, riding on the chariot of the mind, were able to go.\" An\\nalternate reading gives us {.sy 168}cinta-y�n��\" instead of \"citta-y�n��\".\\nThe meaning, however, remains the same. �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 10.44.15 was\\nspoken by the women of Mathur� City.\\n\\n"
