      "content": "\\n\\n     In this way the �lambana of srngara-rasa has been described. Now the\\nudd�panas will be described. Included among the udd�panas are Lord K���a's\\nqualities, such as His ability to charm women (n�r�-moahana-��latva), The\\nhandsome charm of His bodily color, sweetness, fragrance, touch, sound,\\nauspicious qualities, and new youthfulness (avayava-var�a-rasa-gandha-\\nspar�a-�abda-sal-lak�a�a-nava-yauvan�n�� kaman�yat�), His being always new\\nand fresh (nitya-n�tanatva), His making the gop�s fall in love with Him\\n(abhivyakta-bh�vatva), His being controlled by His devotees' love (prema-\\nva�yatva), and His genius (saubuddhya-pratibh�tva). His ability to charm\\nwomen is described in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.21.12):\\n\\n\\nk���a� nir�k�ya vanitotsava-r�pa-��lam. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"K���a's beauty and character create a festival for all women. Indeed,\\nwhen the demigods' wives flying in airplanes with their husbands catch\\nsight of Him and hear His resonant flute-song, their hearts are shaken by\\nCupid, and they become so bewildered that the flowers fall out of their\\nhair and their belts loosen.\"***\\n\\n     The meaning of this verse is clear. This verse was spoken by the\\ngoddesslike gop�s of Vraja.\\n\\n\\nAnucchedas 290-294\\n\\n\\n     Lord K���a's being eternally new and fresh is described in these words\\nof �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (1.11.34):\\n\\n\\nyadyapy asau p�r�va-gata�. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"Although Lord �r� K���a was constantly by their sides, as well as\\nexclusively alone, His feet appeared to them to be newer and newer. The\\ngoddess of fortune, although by nature always restless and moving, could\\nnot quit the Lord's feet. So what woman can be detached from those feet,\\nhaving once taken shelter of them?\"***\\n\\n     Now Lord K���a's quality of making the gop�s fall in love with Him\\nwill be described. The p�rva-r�ga (first stages of that love) is described\\nin these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.31.2):\\n\\n\\n�arad-ud��aye s�dhu j�ta-sat-\\n     sarasijodara-�r�-mu�� d���\\nsurata-n�tha te '�ulka-d�sik�\\n     vara-da nighnato neha kim vadha�\\n\\n\\n     \"O Lord of love, in beauty Your glance excels the whorl of the finest,\\nmost perfec fly formed lotus within the autumn pond. O bestower of\\nbenedictions, You are killing the maidservants who have given themselves to\\nYou freely, without any price. Isn't this murder?\"***\\n\\n     In this verse the words \"d��� surata-n�tha\" mean \"O Lord who with Your\\nglance beg to enjoyamorous pastimes\", \"vara-prada\" means \"O Lord who at the\\nend of our worship of Goddess K�ty�yan� granted the boon we prayed to\\nattain\", \"d��� a�ulka-d�sik�\" mean {.sy 168}without giving any money to\\npurchase us, simply by casting Your love-filled galnce on us, You turned us\\ninto Your slavea\", and \"nighnato neha kim vadha�\" mean \"did You not murder\\nus women?\" In this way this verse shows that simply with His glance Lord\\nK���a enchanted the gop�s. He enchanted them in two ways: 1. He enchanted\\nthem with His form and qualities (svar�pa), and 2. He enchanted them with\\nHis activities others have no power to perform (du�kara-kriy�). In this\\nverse these two ways of enchantement are both described. Lord K���a's\\nenchanting the gop�s is also described in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(10.31.8):\\n\\n\\nmadhuray� gir� valgu-v�kyay�\\n     budha-manoj�ay� pu�karek�a�a\\nvidhi-kar�r im� v�ra muhyat�r\\n     adhara-s�dhun�py�yayasva na�\\n\\n\\n     \"O lotus-eyed one, Your sweet voice and charming words, which attract\\nthe minds of the intelligent, are bewildering us more and more. Our dear\\nhero, please revive Your maidservants with the nectar of Your lips.\"***\\n\\n     In this verse the word \"madhuray�\" means {.sy 168}with the sweetness\\nof Your form\", \"valgu-v�kyay�\" means \"with the sweetness of Your words\",\\nand {.sy 168}budha-manoj�ay�\" means \"which charm the hearts of the\\nintelligent\". In this way Lord K���a's sweetness is manifest. Lord K���a's\\nenchanting the gop�s is also described in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(10.31.10):\\n\\n\\nprahasita� priya-prema-v�k�a�a�\\n     vihara�a� ca te dhy�na-ma�galam\\nrahasi sa�vido y� h�di sp��a�\\n     kuhaka no mana� k�obhayanti hi\\n\\n\\n     \"Your smiles, Your sweet, loving glances, the intimate pastimes and\\nconfidential talks we enjoyed with You--all these are auspicious to\\nmeditate upon, and they touch our hearts. But at the same time, O deceiver,\\nthey very much agitate our minds.\"***\\n\\n     In this verse the word \"samvida�\" means {.sy 168}joking words\".\\n\\n     Lord K���a's enchanting the gop�s is also described in these words of\\n�r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.31.12):\\n\\n\\ndina-parik�aye n�la-kuntalair\\n     vanaruh�nana� bibhrad �v�tam\\nghana-rajasvala� dar�ayan muhur\\n     manasi na� smaram vira yacchasi\\n\\n\\n     \"At the end of the day You repeatedly show us Your lotus face, covered\\nwith dark blue locks of hair and thickly powdered with dust. Thus, O hero,\\nYou arouse lusty desires in our minds.\"***\\n\\n     In this verse the word \"muhu�\" means \"again and again\". Lord K���a's\\nenchanting the gop�s is also described in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(10.31.16-17):\\n\\n\\npati-sut�nvaya-bhr�t�-b�ndhav�n\\n     ativila�ghya te 'nty acyutagata�\\ngati-vidas tavodg�ta-mohit��\\n     kitava yo�ita� kas tyajen ni�i\\n\\n\\n     \"Dear Acyuta, You know very well why we have come here. Who but a\\ncheater like You would abandon young women who come to see Him in the\\nmiddle of the night, enchanted by the loud song of His flute? Just to see\\nYou, we have completely rejected our husbands, children, ancestors,\\nbrothers and other relatives.***\\n\\n\\nrahasi sa�vida� h�c-chayodayam\\n     prahasit�nana� prema-v�k�a�am\\nbrhad-ura� �riyo v�k�ya dh�ma te\\n     muhur ati-sp�h� muhyate mana�\\n\\n\\n     \"Our minds are repeatedly bewildered as we think of the intimate\\nconversations we had with You in secret, feel the rise of lust in our\\nhearts and remember Your smiling lace, Your loving glances and Your broad\\nchest, the resting place of the goddess of fortune. Thus we experience the\\nmost severe hankering for You.\"***\\n\\n     In these verses the words \"gati-vidas tavodg�ta-mohit��\" mean \"You\\nplayed on Your flute, a flute that well knows how to bring us under its\\nspell\". These verses were spoken by the gop�s to the Supreme Personality of\\nGodhead, who at that moment was not visible before them.\\n\\n"
