      "content": "\\n\\n     Lord K���a's enchanting the gop�s in the stage of p�rva-r�ga\\n(beginning of love) is described in these words of Skanda Pur��a, Rev�-\\nkha��a, Tulas�-stava:\\n\\n\\ngav�� hit�ya tulasi\\n     gop�n�� rati-hetave\\nv�nd�vane tva� v�pit�\\n     sevita vi��un� svayam\\n\\n\\n     \"To bring auspiciousness to the cows, as well as to make the gop�s\\nfall in love with Him, Lord Vi��u personally plants You in V�nd�vana and\\nserves you, O Goddess Tulas�.\"\\n     Lord K���a's enhcanting the gop�s while directly enjoying pastimes\\nthem is described in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.29.42):\\n\\n\\niti viklavita� t�s�m. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"Smiling upon hearing these despondent words from the gopis, Lord\\nK���a, the supreme master of all masters of mystic yoga, mercifully enjoyed\\nwith them, although He is self-satisfied.\"***\\n\\n     In this verse the word \"prahasya\" (smiling) describes how Lord K���a\\nenchanted the gop�s.\\n\\n     Lord K���a enchanting the gop�s as He enjoyed pastimes with them is\\nagain described in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.29.43, 44, and 46):\\n\\n\\n\\nt�bhi� samet�bhir ud�ra-ce��ita�. . .\\n . . .ud�ra-h�sa-dvija-kunda-d�dhati�\\n\\n\\n     \"Among the assembled gop�s, the infallible Lord K���a appeared just\\nlike the moon surrounded by stars. He whose activities are so magnanimous\\nmade their faces blossom with His affectionate glances, and His broad\\nsmiles revealed the effulgence of His jasmine-bud-like teeth.***\\n\\n\\nupag�yam�na�. . .udg�yan\\n\\n\\n     \"As the gop�s sang His praises, that leader of hundreds of women sang\\nloudly in reply. He moved among them, wearing His Varjayant� garland,\\nbeautifying the V�nd�vana forest.***\\n\\n\\nb�hu-pras�ra. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"K���a threw His arms around the gop�s and embraced them. He aroused\\nCupid in the beautiful young ladies of Vraja by touching their hands, hair,\\nthighs, belts, and breasts, by playfully scratching them with His\\nfingernails, and also by joking with them, glancing at them, and laughing\\nwith them. In this way the Lord enjoyed His pastimes.\"***\\n\\n     In this way is described Lord K���a's quality of making the gop�s fall\\nin love with Him.\\n\\n     Now will be considered Lord K���a's quality of controlled by His\\ndevotees' love (prema-va�yatva). This quality is of two kinds: 1. being\\ncontrolled by the love of devotees other than His beloveds (prem�ntare�a),\\nand 2. being controlled by the love of His beloveds (preyas�-prem��). The\\nfirst of these (being controlled by the love of devotees other than His\\nbeloveds) is seen in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.35.20):\\n\\n\\nnarma-da� pra�ayi��� vijah�ra\\n\\n\\n      \"O sinless Ya�od�, your darling child, the son of Mah�r�ja Nanda, has\\nfestively enhanced His attire with a jasmine garland, and He is now playing\\nalong the Yamun� in the company of the cows and cowherd boys, amusing His\\ndear companions. The gentle breeze honors Him with its soothing fragrance\\nof sandalwood, while the various Upadevas, standing on all sides like\\npanegyrists, offer their music, singing and gifts of tribute.\"***\\n\\n     Now the second of these (being controlled by the love of His beloveds)\\nwill be considered. This quality when manifested in the stage of p�rva-r�ga\\nis seen in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.53.2):\\n\\n\\ntath�ham api tac-citto\\n     nidr�� ca na labhe ni�i\\n\\n\\n     \"Just as Rukmi��'s mind is fixed on Me, My mind is fixed on her. I\\ncan't even sleep at night.\"***\\n\\n     The meaning of this verse is clear. This verse was spoken by the\\nSupreme Personality of Godhead to Rukmi��'s messenger.\\n\\n\\nAnucchedas 296 and 297\\n\\n\\n     Lord K���a's being controlled by the love of His beloveds in the stage\\nof p�rva-r�ga is also seen in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.29.1):\\n\\n\\nbhagav�n api t� r�tr��\\n     ��radotphulla-mallika�\\nv�k�ya rantu� mana� cakre\\n     yoga-m�y�m up��ritah\\n\\n\\n     \"�r� K���a is the Supreme Personality of Godhead, full in all\\nopulences, yet upon seeing those autumn nights scented with blossoming\\njasmine flowers, He turned His mind toward loving affairs. To fulfill His\\npurposes He employed His internal potency.\"***\\n\\n     In this verse the word \"yoga-m�y�m up��rita�\" means \"taking shelter of\\nyoga-m�y�, which fulfills the numberless desires of numberless gop�s.\"\\n\\n     Lord K���a's being controlled by the love of His beloveds as He\\ndirectly enjoys pastimes with them is seen in these words of �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (10.29.42):\\n\\n\\niti viklavita� t�s��\\n     �rutv� yoge�vare�vara�\\nprahasya sa-daya� gop�r\\n     �tm�r�mo py ar�ramat\\n\\n\\n     \"Smiling upon hearing these despondent words from the gopis, Lord\\nK���a, the supreme master of all masters of mystic yoga, mercifully enjoyed\\nwith them, although He is self-satisfied.\"***\\n\\n     In this verse the word \"viklavitam\" means {.sy 168}the gs' appeals of\\nlove\", \"sadayam\" means {.sy 168}merciful because He was controlled by their\\nlove\", {.sy 168}�tm�r�mo 'pi\" means \"even though He was self-satisfied, He\\ncould see the great virtue of their love for Him\". The word \"�tm�r�ma\"\\n(self-satisfied is also seen in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (1.7.10):\\n\\n�tm�r�m�� ca munaya�. . .\\n . . .ittham-bh�ta-gu�o hari�\\n\\n\\n     \"All different varieties of �tm�r�mas [those who take pleasure in\\n�tm�, or spirit self], especially those established on the path of seff-\\nrealization, though freed from all kinds of material bondage, desire to\\nrender unalloyed devotional service unto the Personality of Godhead. This\\nmeans that the Lord possesses transcendental qualities and therefore can\\nattract everyone, including liberated souls.\"*\\n\\n     The two verses �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 10.29.1 and 10.29.42 were spoken by\\n�r�la �ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n\\nAnucchedas 298 and 299\\n\\n\\n     Lord K���a's being controlled by the love of His beloveds as He\\ndirectly enjoys pastimes with them is also seen in these words of �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (10.33.23):\\n\\n\\nreme svaya� sva-ratir atra gajendra-l�la�\\n\\n\\n     \"My dear King, in the water K���a found Himself being splashed on all\\nsides by the laughing gop�s, who looked at Him with love. As the demigods\\nworshiped Him by showering flowers from their airplanes, the self-satisfied\\nLord took pleasure in playing like the king of the elephants.\"***\\n\\n     In this verse the word \"sva-rati�\" means {.sy 168}Lord K���a who loved\\n(rati) the gop�s (sva)\". Lord K���a's being controlled by the love of His\\nbeloveds as He directly enjoys pastimes with them is also seen in these\\nwords of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.33.20):\\n\\n\\nt�s�� rati-vih�re�a\\n\\n\\n     \"Seeing that the gop�s were fatigued from conjugal enjoyment, my dear\\nKing, merciful K���a lovingly wiped their faces with His comforting\\nhand.\"***\\n\\n     This pastime is also seen in these words of Vi��u Pur��a (5.13.54):\\n\\n\\ngop�-kapola-sa��le�a. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"Lord K���a wiped the gop�s' cheeks.\"\\n\\n     Lord K���a's pastimes with the gop�s are also seen in these words of\\n�r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.33.16):\\n\\n\\neva� pari�va�ga-kar�bhimar�a-\\n     snigdhek�a�oddama-vilasa-hasai�\\nreme rame�o vraja-sundar�bhir\\n     yath�rbhaka� sva-pratibimba-vibhrama�\\n\\n\\n     \"In this way Lord K���a, the original Lord N�r�ya�a, master of the\\ngoddess of fortune, took pleasure in the company of the young women of\\nVraja by embracing them, caressing them and glancing lovingly at them as He\\nsmiled His broad, playful smiles. It was just as if a child were playing\\nwith his own reflection.\"***\\n\\n     Here the word \"rame�a\" means \"the controller of Goddess Lak�m�\". This\\nverse says: \"by embracing them, caressing them and glancing lovingly at\\nthem, Lord K���a enjoyed pastimes with the gop�s\". In this way Lord K���a\\nwas controlled by the gop�s' love. Here is given the example of a\\nchildplaying with his reflection. As a child plays with his reflection, so\\nLord K���a enjoyed pastimes beginnign with singing and dancing with the\\ngop�s. In this activities it is seen that Lord K���a and the gop�s were\\ndeeply attached to each other.\\n\\n"
