      "content": "\\n\\n     Then it is said in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.33.25):\\n\\n\\neva� �a���k���u-vir�jit� ni���\\n     sa satya-k�mo 'nurat�bal�-ga�a�\\nsi�eva �tmany avaruddha-saurata�\\n     sarv�� �arat-k�vya-kath�-ras��ray�h\\n\\n\\n     \"Although the gop�s were firmly attached to Lord K���a, whose desires\\nare always fulfilled, the Lord was not internally affected by any mundane\\nsex desire. Still, to perform His pastimes the Lord took advantage of all\\nthose moonlit autumn nights, which inspire poetic descriptions of\\ntranscendental affairs.\"***\\n\\n     In this verse the word \"evam\" means \"as was previously described\",\\n\"anurat�bal�-ga�a�\" means {.sy 168}the gop�s who loved K���a eternally\",\\n\"sa�\" means \"�r� K���acandra\", \"�tmany avaruddha-saurata�\" means \"whose\\nthoughts were filled with flirting and various amorous pastimes\", \"satya-\\nk�ma�\" means {.sy 168}whose love is never wrong\", \"�arat-k�vya-kath�-\\nras��ray��\" means \"nectar poems in relation to autumn\", \"sarv��\" means\\n\"them all\", and \"si�eve\" means \"He utilized\". The wird \"�arat\" here may\\nalso mean \"for an entire year\". The word {.sy 168}�a���k���u-vir�jit�\"\\n(moonlit nights) further describes this pastime. The Lord's amorous\\npastimes are also seen in the following owrds of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(10.60.58):\\n\\n\\neva� saurata-saml�pai�. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"And so the self-satisfied Supreme Lord of the universe enjoyedwith\\nthe goddess of fortune, engaging her in lovers' talks and thus imitating\\nthe ways of human society.\"***\\n\\n     This verse describes Lord K���a's pastimes of joking with Rukmi��. The\\nword \"saurata\" here has the same meaning it had in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n10.33.25. �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 10.33.25 was spoken by �r�la �ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
