      "sourceStartLine": 19106,
      "content": "\\n\\n     In the matter of His relationship with the gop�s Lord K���a Himself\\ndeclares in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.32.22):\\n\\n\\nna p�raye 'ham. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"I am not able to repay My debt for your spotless service, even within\\na lifetime of Brahm�. Your connection with Me is beyond reproach. You have\\nworshiped Me, cutting off all domestic ties, which are difficult to break.\\nTherefore please let your own glorious deeds be your compensation.\"*\\n\\n     Lord K���a's separation from the gop�s when He went to live in a\\nfaraway place is described in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.46.1-4):\\n\\n\\nv����n�� pravaro mantr�\\n     k���asya dayita� sakh�\\n�i�yo b�haspate� s�k��d\\n     uddhavo buddhi-sattama�\\n\\n\\n     \"The supremely intelligent Uddhava was the best counselor of the V���i\\ndynasty, a beloved friend of Lord �r� K���a, and a direct disciple of\\nB�haspati.***\\n\\n\\ntam �ha bhagav�n pre��ha�\\n     bhaktam ek�ntina� kvacit\\ng�h�tv� p��in� p��i�\\n     prapann�rti-haro hari�\\n\\n\\n     \"The Supreme Lord Hari, who relieves the distress of all who surrender\\nto Him, once took the hand of His fully devoted, dearmost friend Uddhava\\nand addressed him as follows.***\\n\\n\\ngacchoddhava vraja� saumya\\n     pitror nau pr�tim �vaha\\ngop�n�� mad-viyog�dhi�\\n     mat-sande�air vimocaya\\n\\n\\n     \"Dear gentle Uddhava, go to Vraja and give pleasure to Our parents.\\nAnd also relieve the gop�s, suffering in separation from Me, by giving them\\nMy message.***\\n\\n\\nt� man-manask� mat-pr���\\n     mad-arthe tyakta-daihik��\\n\\n\\n     \"The minds of those gop�s are always absorbed in Me, and their very\\nlives are ever devoted to Me. For My sake they have abandoned everything\\nrelated to their bodies.\"***\\n\\n     This pastime is also described in the Skanda Pur��a, Prahl�da-sa�hit�,\\nDv�rak�-m�h�tmya, where �r�m�n Uddhava tells the gop�s:\\n\\n\\nbhagav�n api d��arha�\\n     kandarpa-�ara-p��ita�\\nna bhu�kte na �vapiti ca\\n     cintayan vo hy ahar-ni�am\\n\\n\\n     \"Wounded by K�madeva's arrow, Lord K���a thinks of you gop�s day and\\nnight. He neither eats nor sleeps.\"\\n\\n     Most of the princesses married by Lord K���a had previously been gop�s\\nin Vraja. As time passed in separation from K���a, they became those\\nprincesses to save themselves from committing suicide in despair. This is\\ndescribed in the following words of Padma Pur��a:\\n\\n\\nkai�ora gopa-kany�s t�\\n     yauvane r�ja-kanyak��\\n\\n\\n     \"The girls who in the beginning of their youth had been gop�s at the\\nlater stage of their youth became princesses.\"\\n\\n     That the Lord's beloveds are inclined to commit suicide rather than\\nlive without Lord K���a is seen in these words spoken by Queen Rukmi�� in\\n�r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.52.43):\\n\\n\\nyarhy ambuj�k�a na labheya bhavat-pras�da�\\n     jahy�m as�n vrata-k���n �ata-janmabhi� sy�t\\n\\n\\n     \"O lotus-eyed one, if I cannot obtain Your mercy, I shall simply give\\nup my vital force, which will have become weak from severe penances I will\\nperform. Then, after hundreds of lifetimes of endeavor, I may obtain Your\\nmercy.\"***\\n\\n"
