      "sourceStartLine": 19207,
      "content": "\\n\\n     Amongst the udd�panas is Lord K���a's caste status. Lord K���a's caste\\nas a gopa is described in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.35.14):\\n\\n\\nvividha-gopa-cara�e�u vidagdho\\n     ve�u-v�dya urudh�. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"O pious mother Ya�od�, your son, who is expert in all the arts of\\nherding cows, has invented many new styles of flute-playing. When He takes\\nHis flute to His bimba-red lips and sends forth the tones of the harmonic\\nscale in variegated melodies, Brahm�, Siva, Indra and other chief demigods\\nbecome confused upon hearing the sound. Although they are the most learned\\nauthorities, they cannot ascertain the essence of that music, and thus they\\nbow down their heads and hearts.\"***\\n\\n     The meaning of this verse is clear. This verse was spoken by the\\ngoddesslike gop�s of Vraja.\\n\\n"
