      "headingType": "anuccheda",
      "sourceStartLine": 19230,
      "content": "\\n\\n     Lord K���a's caste as one of the Y�davas, a k�atriya, is seen in these\\nwords of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.90.20):\\n\\n\\nmegha �r�m��s tvam asi dayito y�davendrasya n�nam. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"O revered cloud, you are indeed dear to the chief of the Yadus, who\\nbears the mark of �r�vatsa. Like us, you are bound to Him by love and are\\nmeditating upon Him. Your heart is distraught with great eagerness, as our\\nhearts are, and as you remember Him again and again you shed a torrent of\\ntears. Association with K���a brings such misery!\"***\\n\\n     The meaning of this verse is clear. This verse was spoken by the\\nLord's queens.\\n\\n"
