      "content": "\\n     Now Lord K���a's activities (kriy�) will be considered. The Lord's\\nactivities are of two kinds: 1. bh�va-sambandhin� (activities of love), and\\n2. sv�bh�vika-vinodamaya (pastimes that come from His own nature). The\\nfirst of these two kinds of activities (activities of love) is described in\\nthese words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.29.4):\\n\\n\\nni�amya g�ta� tad ana�ga-vardhanam. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"When the young women of V�nd�vana heard K���a's flute song, which\\narouses romantic feelings, their minds were captivated by the Lord. They\\nwent to where their lover waited, each unknown to the others, moving so\\nquickly that their earrings swung back and forth.\"***\\n\\n     The meaning of this verse is clear. This verse was spoken by �r�la\\n�ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
