      "content": "\\n\\n     The second of these two kinds of activities (pastiems that come from\\nHis own nature) is described in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.35.2):\\n\\n\\n\\nv�ma-b�hu-k�ta-v�ma-kapolo\\n     valgita-bhrur adhar�rpita-ve�um. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"When Mukunda vibrates the flute He has placed to His lips, stopping\\nits holes with His tender fingers, He rests His left cheek on His left arm\\nand makes His eyebrows dance. At that time the demigoddesses traveling in\\nthe sky with their husbands, the Siddhas, become amazed. As those ladies\\nlisten, they are embarrassed to find their minds yielding to the pursuit of\\nlusty desires, and in their distress they are unaware that the belts of\\ntheir garments are loosening.\"***\\n\\n     The meaning of this verse is clear. This verse was spoken by the\\ngoddesslike gop�s of Vraja.\\n\\n"
