      "content": "\\n\\n     These activities are also seen in the following words of �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (10.35.14):\\n\\n\\nvividha-gopa-cara�e�u. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"O pious mother Ya�od�, your son, who is expert in all the arts of\\nherding cows, has invented many new styles of flute-playing. When He takes\\nHis flute to His bimba-red lips and sends forth the tones of the harmonic\\nscale in variegated melodies, Brahm�, Siva, Indra and other chief demigods\\nbecome confused upon hearing the sound. Although they are the most learned\\nauthorities, they cannot ascertain the essence of that music, and thus they\\nbow down their heads and hearts.\"***\\n\\n     Now the Lord's paraphernalia (dravya) will be considered. Amongst them\\nare the Lord's beloveds, who are described in these words of �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (10.22.6):\\n\\n\\nu�asy utth�ya gotrai� svair\\n     anyony�baddha-b�hava�\\nk���am uccair jagur y�ntya�\\n     k�lindy�� sn�tum anvaham\\n\\n\\n     \"Each day they rose at dawn. Calling out to one another by name, they\\nall held hands and loudly sang the glories of K���a while going to the\\nK�lind� to take their bath.\"***\\n\\n     In this verse the word \"gotrai�\" means {.sy 168}in various groups\".\\nThis verse was spoken by �r�la �ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
