      "content": "\\n\\n     Vil�sa-anubh�va is described in these words of Ujjvala-n�lama�i,\\nAnubh�va-prakara�a, Text 27:\\n\\n\\ngati-sth�n�san�d�n��\\n     mukha-netr�di-karma��m\\ntat-k�lika� tu vai�i��ya�\\n     vil�sa� priya-sa�gajam\\n\\n\\n     \"The graceful gestures of the face, eyes, and other parts of the body\\nwhile walking, sitting, standing, and enjoying various pastimes with the\\nbeloved Lord K���a are called vil�sa.\"\\n\\n     Vil�sa is seen in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.32.3):\\n\\n\\nta� viloky�gata� pre��ha�\\n     pr�ty-utphulla-d��o 'bal��\\n\\n\\n     \"When the gop�s saw that their dearmost K���a had returned to them,\\nthey all stood up at once, and out of their affection for Him their eyes\\nbloomed wide. It was as if the air of life had reentered their bodies.\"***\\n\\n     The meaning of this verse is clear. This verse was spoken by �r�la\\n�ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
