      "content": "\\n\\n     Vibhrama is described in these words of Ujjvala-n�lama�i, Anubh�va-\\nprakara�a, Text 34:\\n\\n�r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.22.15):\\n\\n\\nvallabha-pr�pti-vel�y��\\n     madan�ve�a-sambhram�t\\nvibhramo h�ra-m�ly�di-\\n     bh���-sth�na-viparyaya�\\n\\n\\n     \"Hastily preparing to meet her lover, the bewildered heroine may place\\nher necklace, flower-garland, and other ornaments in the wrong places. This\\nis called vibhrama.\"\\n\\n     Vibhrama is seen in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.29.7):\\n\\n\\nvyatyasta-vastr�bhara���\\n     k��cit k����ntika� yayu�\\n\\n\\n     \"Though their clothes and ornaments were in complete disarray, the gs\\nrushed off to K���a.\"***\\n\\n     Vibboka is described in these words of Ujjvala-n�lama�i, Anubh�va-\\nprakara�a, Text 47:\\n\\n\\ni��e 'pi garva-m�n�bhy��\\n     vibboka� sy�d an�dara�\\n\\n\\n     \"Even though pleased by Lord K���a's gift, the heroine may angrily and\\nproudly pretend to dislike it. This is called vibboka.\"\\n\\n     Vibboka is seen in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.32.6):\\n\\n\\nek� bhru-ku�im �badhya. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"One gop�, beside herself with loving anger, bit her lips and stared\\nat Him with frowning eyebrows, as if to wound Him with her harsh\\nglances.\"***\\n\\n     Lalita is described in these words of Ujjvala-n�lama�i, Anubh�va-\\nprakara�a, Text 51:\\n\\n\\nviny�sa-bha�gir a�g�n��\\n     bhr�-vil�sa-manohar�\\nsukum�r� bhaved yatra\\n     lalita� tad ud�h�tam\\n\\n\\n     \"Playful, enchanting movements of the eyebrows, and graceful, delicate\\nmovements of the limbs are called lalita.\"\\n\\n     In this eay these features of ecstatic love should be u understood.\\n�r�mad-Bh�gavatam 10.29.7 quoted in this anuccheda was spoken by �r�la\\n�ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
