      "sourceStartLine": 20336,
      "content": "\\n\\n     Vil�pa is described in these words of Ujjvala-n�lama�i, Anubh�va-\\nprakara�a, Text 75:\\n\\n\\nvil�po du�kha-ja� vaca�\\n\\n\\n     \"Vil�pa means `words born of suffering'.\"\\n\\n     Vil�pa is seen in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.47.47):\\n\\n\\npara� saukhya� hi nairasyam. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"Indeed, the greatest happiness is to renounce all desires, as even\\nthe prostitute Pi�gal� has declared. Yet even though we know this, we\\ncannot give up our hopes of attaining K���a.\"***\\n\\n     The meaning of this verse is clear. This verse was spoken by the\\ngop�s.\\n\\n"
