mal�. She is the\\neighth gop�. She is described in these words of Vi��u Pur��a:\\n\\n\\nk�cid �y�ntam �lokya\\n     govinda-mati-har�it�\\nk���a k��eti k���eti\\n     pr�ha n�nyad udairayat\\n\\n\\n     \"When she saw Lord K���a approasch, her heart became joyful. She\\ncalled out, `K���a! K���a! K���a!' She spoke no word but that.\"\\n\\n     Another famous gop� is named Bhadr�. The gop�s' blissful love for Lord\\nK���a is seen in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 10.32.9:\\n\\n\\nsarv��. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"All the gop�s enjoyed the greatest festivity when they saw their\\nbeloved Ke�ava again. They gave up the distress of separation, just as\\npeople in general forget their misery when they gain the association of a\\nspiritually enlightened person.\"***\\n\\n     The verses of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 10.32.4-9 were spoken by �r�la\\n�ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
