      "content": "\\n\\n     Sending a love-letter (k�ma-lekh�) is one of the activities of p�rva-\\nr�ga. An example of a love-letter is seen in these words of �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (10.52.37):\\n\\n\\n�rutv� gu��n bhuvana-sundara ���vat�� te. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"�r� Rukmi�� said (in her letter read by the brahmana): O beauty of\\nthe worlds, having heard of Your qualities, which enter the ears of those\\nwho hear and remove their bodily distress, and havong alos heard of Your\\nbeauty, which fulfills all the visual desires of those who see, I have\\nfixed my shameless mind upon You, O K���a.\"***\\n\\n     After p�rva-r�ga comes sambhoga. Sambhoga has four parts: 1.\\nsandar�ana (gazing), 2. sa�jalpa (conversation), 3. samspar�a (touching),\\nand 4. samprayoga (union). Sandar�ana means \"gazing\". An example of\\nsambhoga characterized by gazing and touching is seen in these words of\\n�r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.52.54-55):\\n\\n\\nsaiva� �anai� calayat� cala-padma-ko�au\\n     pr�pti� tad� bhagavata� prasam�k�am�n�\\nuts�rya v�ma-karajair alak�n ap��gai�\\n     pr�ptan hriyaik�ata n�p�n dad��e 'cyuta� ca\\n\\nt�� r�ja-kany�� ratham �ruruk�at��\\n     jah�ra k���o dvi�at�� sam�k�at�m\\n\\n\\n     \"On the pretext of the procession, Rukmi�� displayed her beauty for\\nK���a alone. Slowly she advanced the two moving lotus-whorls of her feet,\\nawaiting the arrival of the Supreme Lord. With the fingernails of her left\\nhad she pushed some strands of hair away from her facw and shyly looked\\nfrom the corners of her eyes\\n\\n.mt 3\\n.mb 5\\n.rm 6.5 in Set Right Margin to 6.5 in.\\n.rm 65\\n..\\n      Select font 1\\n.fa times to Times Roman type style.\\n.lh 1.25 em\\n.ch 12 pt\\n\\n.fa timesitl\\n.lh 1.25 em\\n.ch 12 pt\\n..\\n\\n.fa clarendo\\n.ch 12 pt\\n..\\n\\n.fa helvetic\\n.ch 16 pt\\n..\\n\\n.fa clarendo\\n.ch 16.2 pt\\n..\\n\\n.fa clarendo\\n.ch 23 pt\\n..\\n\\n.. Lower case Italicized\\n.de  {.px -1.2 en}{.py +0.23 em}.{.py -.23 em}\\n.. ^D - . below letters n - h 