ithin for a long time. In this way they\\nfionally gave up the pain of separation from Him, just as sagesa give up\\nthe anxiety of false ego by embracing their innermost consciousness.\"***\\n\\n     In this verse (�r�mad-Bh�gavatam 10.23.23) the word {.sy\\n168}abhimataya�\" means: \"false ego\", and the phrase {.sy 168}prajnam tapam\\nvijahu�\" means \"as the sages, situated in spiritual trace, become free of\\nall sufferings, so these women also became free of all sufferings\".\\n\\n     One of those br�hma��s, becoming free of their previous\\ndisqualifications, attained in her heart p�rva-r�ga love for Lord K���a and\\nthen enjoyed sambhoga pastimes with Him, pastimes that begin with touching\\nHim. This attainment of hers is seen in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam\\n(10.23.35):\\n\\n\\ntatraik� vidh�t� bhartr�\\n     bhagavanta� yath�-�rutam\\nh�dopaguhya vijahau\\n     deha� karm�nubandhanam\\n\\n\\n     \"One of ther ladies had been forcibly kept back by her husband. When\\nshe heard the others describe the Supreme Lord K���a, she embraced him\\nwithin her heart and gave up her material body, the basis of bondage to\\nmaterial activity.\"***\\n\\n     When she gave up the brahmana body she had attained by past karma,\\nthen he disqualification was destroyed and she was able to embrace Lord\\nK���a in her heart. In that way she attained Lord K���a's association. This\\nis described in these words of Bhagavad-g�t� (8.6):\\n\\n\\nya� ya� v�pi smana bh�vam. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"Whatever state of being one remembers when he quits this body, O son\\nof Kunt�, that state he will attain without fail.\"*\\n\\n     The statement that she attained Lord K���a's association means that\\nshe attained the form of a gop�. She did not attain the form of a br�hma��\\nand in that form associate with Lord K���a. That Lord K���a's close\\nassociates were all cowherd people is seen in these words of �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (10.23.37):\\n\\n\\neva� l�l�-nara-vapu�. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"Thus the Supreme Lord, appearing like a human being to perform His\\npastimes, imitated the ways of human society. He enjoyed pleasing His cows,\\ncowherd boyfriends and cowherd girlfriends with His beauty, words, and\\nactions.\"***\\n\\n     In this verse it is said that Lord K���a enjoyed pleasing the cows and\\ncowherd people. He did not enjoy pastimes with others, at least not in the\\nland of Vraja. In Vraja that yaj�a-patn� could not enjoy pastimes with Lord\\nK���a without becoming a gop�. She thus entered the Vraja that is not\\nmanifested in the material world. In that unmanifested Vraja Lord K���a\\nenjoys many different pastimes, pastimes without limit. This is explained\\nin the K���a-sandarbha. Therefore there is nothing wrong in her death. She\\nyearned to attain Lord K���a. With a great effort she struggled to attain\\nHim. In that way she attained a very exalted relationship (rasa) with Him.\\n�r�mad-Bh�gavatam 10.23.35 quoted above was spoken by �r�la �ukadeva\\nGosv�m�.\\n\\n"
