      "content": "\\n\\n     D�ra-prava�a manifested in the past is seen in these words spoken by\\nLord K���a in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.46.4):\\n\\n\\nt� man-manask� mat-pr���\\n     mad-arthe tyakta-daihik��. . .\\n\\n\\n     \"The minds of those gop�s are always absorbed in Me, and their very\\nlives are veer devoted to Me. For My sake they have abandoned everything\\nrelated to their bodies.\"***\\n\\n     In this kind of prav�sa there are written letters between the lover\\nand beloved and there are also messages orally repeated by a messnger. The\\nmessengers here may be Lord Balar�ma, Uddhava, or other friends of Lord\\nK���a. An example of such a messenger is seen in these words of �r�mad-\\nBh�gavatam (10.47.3):\\n\\n\\nta� pra�raye��vanata� su-sat-k�ta�\\n     sa-vr��a-h�sek�a�a-sun�t�dibhi�\\n\\n\\n     \"Bowing their herads in humility, the gop�s duly honored Uddhava with\\ntheir shy, smiling glances and pleasing words. They took him to a quiet\\nplace, seated him, and comfortably began to question him, for they\\nrecognized him to be a messenger fro� K���a, the master of the goddess of\\nfortune.\"***\\n\\n     Although in the past they had kept everything secret, when Uddhava\\narrived, the distraught gop�s abandoned all shyness. This is seen in these\\nwords of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.40.9):\\n\\n\\niti gopyo hi govinde\\n     gata-v�k-k�ya-m�nas��\\nk���a-d�te sam�y�te\\n     uddhave tyakta-laukik��\\n\\n\\n     \"Thus speaking, the gop�s, whose words, bodies, and minds were fully\\ndedicated to Lord Govinda, put aside all their regular work now that\\nK���a's messenger, Uddhava, had arrived among them.\"***\\n\\n     This is also seen in these words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.47.3):\\n\\n\\nap�cchann\\n\\n\\n     \"Bowing their herads in humility, the gop�s duly honored Uddhava with\\ntheir shy, smiling glances and pleasing words. They took him to a quiet\\nplace, seated him, and comfortably began to question him, for they\\nrecognized him to be a messenger from K���a, the master of the goddess of\\nfortune.\"***\\n\\n     In the sequence of verses in �r�mad-Bh�gavatam this verse precedes\\n�r�mad-Bh�gavatam 10.47.9 quoted above. This verse was spoken by �r�la\\n�ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
