      "content": "\\n\\n     In this way the truth of sambhoga, which consists of seeing, touching,\\nand conversing with Lord K���a, is revealed. Lord K���a stayed at\\nKuruk�etra for three months. Then He and the gop�s were again separated.\\nAfter that there were not again separatyion between them. After that they\\nenjoyed sambhoga pastimes together. The conclusion of these pastimes is\\ndescribed in the following words of �r�mad-Bh�gavatam (10.83.1):\\n\\n\\ntath�nug�hya bhagav�n\\n     gop�n�� sa gurur gati�\\n\\n\\n     \"Thus Lord K���a, the spiritual master of the gop�s and the very\\npurpose of their life, showed them His mercy. He then met with Yudhi��hira\\nand all His other relatives and inquired from them about their welfare.\"***\\n\\n     This verse explains that the gop�s attained the desire they expressed\\nin �r�mad-Bh�gavatam 10.82.48. This is seen in this verse, which explains\\nthat Lord K���a gave His mercy (anug�hya) to them. This verse also affirms\\nthat they attained Lord K���a, who is their eternal destination (gati�).\\nThis verse was spoken by �r�la �ukadeva Gosv�m�.\\n\\n"
